\par\par \b \uc2 U.S. Stocks End Broadly Lower\b0\par\par\uc2 877 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 23 Januar 2014\par 13:35\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2014, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 Stocks suffered broad declines as weak data out of China spooked investors, triggering a flight out of riskier assets.\par \par \uc2 The increase in market volatility, which included sharp selloffs in emerging markets and the biggest tumble in Argentina's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in over a decade, came as U.S. stocks has struggled in recent weeks to regain the upward momentum seen at the end of 2013.\par \par \uc2 On Thursday, the Dow Jones Industrial Average slid 175.99 points, or 1.1%, to 16197.35, the lowest close since Dec. 19.\par \par \uc2 The S&P 500 index shed 16.40 points, or 0.9%, to 1828.46, and the Nasdaq Composite Index dropped 24.13 points, or 0.6%, to 4218.87. Materials and financials led declines in all 10 of the S&P 500 sectors.\par \par \uc2 The S&P 500 ended the session 1.1% below its Jan. 15 record-high close.\par \par \uc2 Data showing China's manufacturing activity contracted in January sparked worries that the recent slowing momentum in the world's second-largest economy is carrying over into the new year.\par \par \uc2 That triggered a selloff in riskier emerging-market shares and \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , and helped bolster prices of Treasurys and gold, which are viewed as safe-haven assets.\par \par \uc2 "We had some really weak data out of China, and that's scaring people," said Ian Winer, director of equity trading at Wedbush Securities. He said that since the global rally in equities is predicated on global economic growth, "if you get weakness [in China], it's something [stock] bulls have to question."\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 iShares MSCI Emerging Markets\uc2  exchange-traded fund tumbled 2.5% to the lowest level since September 2013.\par \par \uc2 Several emerging-market \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  also sold off sharply in unison. The Argentine peso suffered the biggest one-day drop against the dollar in a decade, as Argentina faces heightened concerns about its own dwindling foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves. In addition, the Turkish lira sank to another record low against the U.S. dollar. The lira tumbled even after \b \highlight22\uc2 Turkey\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  directly in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets for the first time in two years to slow its fall, raising questions about the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's ability to fight \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  losses.\par \par \uc2 The lack of confidence spilled over into other emerging-market \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , with the Russian ruble and South African rand dropping to multiyear lows against the greenback.\par \par \uc2 "China is still the growth engine of the global economy," said Chris Gaffney, senior market strategist with EverBank Wealth Management, which manages money across asset classes for high-net-worth individuals. "The [\b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 ] sell-off is the result of worries about China's growth, and that's also leading to broader stock-market declines."\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, Treasury prices rallied, with the yield on the 10-year Treasury note settling at 2.774%, the lowest seen since Dec. 3. Yields fall as Treasury prices rise. Front-month January gold futures ran up 1.9% to a two-month high of $1,262.60 an ounce.\par \par \uc2 The attention placed on China and its effect on global risk assets marks a sudden change for investors, who have grown accustomed to focusing on U.S. corporate earnings.\par \par \uc2 "This is the first time in many weeks that we've seen this kind of across-the-board volatility," said Adam Grimes, chief investment officer at Waverly Advisors, which provides tactical research and advisory services to traders and money managers. "There is a clear theme here, that the market doesn't like risk today."\par \par \uc2 Mr. Grimes added that while the selloffs in emerging-market \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  have his immediate attention, in the context of the bigger picture for stocks, he believes nothing has changed.\par \par \uc2 "If this continued for two to three days, then we might be rolling over into a bigger-scale pullback," Mr. Grimes said. But for anyone with a more than one-week view, "this is nothing; it's still business as usual, " he said.\par \par \uc2 In corporate news, U.S.-listed shares of Finland's \uc2 Nokia\uc2  slumped 8.7% after the company said handset sales declined in the fourth quarter. \uc2 Nokia\uc2  is expected to transfer its handset business this quarter to \uc2 Microsoft\uc2  this quarter. \uc2 Microsoft\uc2  shares edged up 0.4%.\par \par \uc2 Also in the Dow, \uc2 McDonald's\uc2  reported flat fourth-quarter earnings and a 0.1% drop in global same-store sales, hurt by a 1.4% decline in U.S. sales.\par \par \uc2 Netflix surged 16% after the provider of streaming videos reported late Wednesday earnings and revenue above analyst forecasts. Leading up to results, the stock had declined 9.4% in the year to date.\par \par \uc2 Economic data were mixed. Weekly jobless claims edged up slightly less than forecast, while sales of existing homes increased less than expected.\par \par \uc2 In Europe, the Stoxx Europe 600 lost 1%, pulling back from a six-year high, as the weak Chinese data overshadowed data showing a pickup in activity in the euro zone.\par \par \uc2 Asian markets fell on the back of the weak Chinese data. China's Shanghai Composite shed 0.5%, after running up 3% over the previous two sessions.\par \par \uc2 Alexandra Scaggs and Nicole Hong contributed to this article.\par \par \uc2 Write to Tomi Kilgore at tomi.kilgore@wsj.com\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 January 23, 2014 07:35 ET (12:35 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020140123ea1n001fq\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
