\par\par \b \uc2 EM Morning Roundup: China's Manufacturing Contracts,  \highlight22\uc2 Turkey Intervenes \highlight\uc2  In  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  Markets -- Barron's Blog\b0\par\par\uc2 By Shuli Ren   \par \uc2 358 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 23 Januar 2014\par 13:31\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2014, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 China:\par \par \uc2 The preliminary \uc2 HSBC\uc2  Purchasing Managers' Index for January was only 49.6. A reading under 50 signals contraction. The Shanghai Stock Market Composite Index lost 0.5%. The Hong Kong Hang Seng Index lost 1.5%.\par \par \uc2 China's manufacturing slowdown brought other north Asian countries' equity indices down as well. Korea's KOSPI Composite Index was down 1.2% and Taiwan's TAIEX Index lost 0.4%.\par \par \uc2 Lenovo has agreed to buy \uc2 IBM\uc2 's low-end, low-margin server business (\uc2 IBM\uc2 ) for $2.3 billion.\par \par \uc2 A U.S. court s uspended the Big Four accounting firms' Chinese joint ventures from auditing U.S.-traded companies for six months. The accounting firms said they would appeal. But if the ruling stands, it could temporarily leave the Chinese companies traded in U.S. without an auditor.\par \par \uc2 China is scrambling to avoid a $500 million loan trust default. This loan trust was originated by one of the largest trust companies and distributed by China's largest bank ICBC to wealthy investors.\par \par \uc2 Japan's \uc2 Fast Retailing\uc2 , which owns the Uniqlo brand, plans to seek a Hong Kong DR listing.\par \par \uc2 India:\par \par \uc2 What's the risk of falling in love with the wrong boy? Being gang raped by 12 Angry Men. The S&P BSE 100 Index was little changed.\par \par \uc2 Thailand:\par \par \uc2 The opposition leader Suthep Thaugsuban defied a state of emergency issued by the government and took to the street protests again. Thailand's Constitutional Court said it would rule whether elections on February 2 would be delayed. The Thailand SET Index rallied 1.4%.\par \par \uc2 Turkey:\par \par \uc2 Turkey issued its first dollar bond this year, raising $2.5 billion amidst healthy demand. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  i ntervened in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  market for the first time in two years to slow the lira's fall. The Turkey ISE 100 Index lost 0.8% this morning.\par \par \uc2 Brazil:\par \par \uc2 CPI inflation unexpectedly slowed in January. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  More at Barrons Emerging Markets blog, \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://blogs.barrons.com/emergingmarketsdaily/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://blogs.barrons.com/emergingmarketsdaily/}}}\par \par \uc2 \f2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 January 23, 2014 07:31 ET (12:31 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020140123ea1n001fn\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
