\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Turkey Intervenes \highlight\uc2  to Halt Lira Slide\b0\par\par\uc2 573 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 23 Januar 2014\par 12:05\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2014, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 ISTANBUL--\b \highlight22\uc2 Turkey\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  directly in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets Thursday for the first time in two years in an effort to slow the lira's free fall.\par \par \uc2 Policy makers in Ankara started selling dollars as the lira hit a record low of 2.2973 against the dollar before noon local time, and slumped to an all-time nadir of 3.1342 against the euro, said three traders familiar with the transaction. The lira bounced back somewhat in response, but didn't immediately recoup all the day's losses.\par \par \uc2 In a one-sentence emailed statement, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said it was \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  with direct \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  sales because of "unhealthy price developments."\par \par \uc2 "This is pretty forceful. And the last time they did this, they didn't do it just once. But these sorts of \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  tend to just give people the opportunity to buy more dollars," said Bartosz Pawlowski, head of emerging market strategy at \uc2 BNP Paribas\uc2  in London.\par \par \uc2 The move comes as Turkey's lira is in its longest losing streak since August 2001, which had triggered an economic crisis and caused the banking system to collapse. To be sure, Turkey is at a much stronger financial position now: the government sold a $2.5 billion bond Wednesday that was four times oversubscribed, the Treasury said Thursday.\par \par \uc2 Still, the sustained lira selloff shows the market's discomfort with the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's refusal to raise benchmark interest rates to curb \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  losses and target inflation. On Tuesday, Governor Erdem Basci did a backdoor increase by announcing a new 9% funding rate that will be applicable in so-called extraordinary days of additional monetary tightening. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is poised to hold the first such day on Monday, and then again on Thursday, which Mr. Basci says will effectively raise borrowing costs.\par \par \uc2 "I think it's just a waiting game. They are trying to keep the lira steady and calm the market down until the 9% funding rate kicks in on Monday," Mr. Pawlowski said.\par \par \uc2 "I expect more high-amount, direct dollar sales, but even if that curbs losses a little bit I do not expect it to have a lasting impact. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  needs to raise interest rates or apply additional monetary tightening more frequently for a sustainable appreciation in the lira," said Gizem Oztok Altinsac, chief economist at Garanti Securities in Istanbul.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has already burned through about $19 billion, a third of its net reserves, in an unsuccessful effort to halt the lira's slide since last June. The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  declined 21% against the dollar last year, making it worst performer in emerging markets, and is leading losses in developing economies with a 7% drop this year.\par \par \uc2 "In essence, the current bag of \uc2 Turkey's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  policies has not been working. It is falling back on more tried and tested methods, and resorting to direct \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , as opposed to selling via managed \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  auctions," said Tim Ash, head of emerging markets strategy at \uc2 Standard Bank PLC\uc2  in London. "This might ultimately slow the pace of depreciation...but it will not change the trend, unless we see some improvements in the underlying drivers of the weak lira."\par \par \uc2 Write to Emre Peker at emre.peker@wsj.com and Yeliz Candemir at yeliz.candemir@wsj.com\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 January 23, 2014 06:05 ET (11:05 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020140123ea1n0016k\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
