\par\par \b \uc2 EMERGING MARKETS-Rouble hits 4-1/2 year low vs basket, lira tests record low\b0\par\par\uc2 534 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 Januar 2014\par 12:04\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2014 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 LONDON, Jan 14 (Reuters) - The rouble hit a 4-1/2 year low against its dollar-euro basket on Tuesday after \uc2 Russia's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said it would scale back its \b \highlight22\uc2 forex interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 , while the lira tested a new record low as \b \highlight22\uc2 Turkey\b0 \highlight\uc2 's current account deficit widened further.\par \par \uc2 Broader emerging markets also slipped, taking their cue from a firmer dollar and Wall Street's 1.2 percent decline late on Monday, with MSCI's main emerging equity index down half a percent.\par \par \uc2 Emerging markets have been under pressure for more than six months on expectations - which become reality this month - that the Federal Reserve will scale back its bond-buying programme, encouraging investors to return home.\par \par \uc2 "A lot of foot-loose institutional capital has gone into emerging markets, and we're not sure that has come out yet," Kevin Gardner, European CIO at \uc2 Barclays\uc2  Wealth, told a briefing.\par \par \uc2 "Markets have cheapened up, but we are not yet too bullish on EM stocks."\par \par \uc2 Russian stocks fell more than 1 percent, but losses in the broader index were tempered by gains in its largest constituent, China. Mainland Chinese shares broke a four-day fall to end 0.9 percent higher.\par \par \uc2 The rouble hit 4-1/2 year lows against its dollar-euro basket and four-month lows against the dollar after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said on Monday it would end 'targeted' \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market as part of a strategic shift towards letting the rouble float freely.\par \par \uc2 The reduction to zero of its \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which had been set at $60 million per day, will increase the flexibility of the exchange rate corridor used by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  and reduce its presence on the market.\par \par \uc2 "As rouble volatility rises, the spot is likely to weaken at current interest rate levels," \uc2 Commerzbank\uc2  analysts wrote in a client note.\par \par \uc2 The lira fell more than half a percent to the dollar and Turkish stocks dropped more than 1 percent following data showing the current account deficit widened to $3.94 billion in November. The widening came in below expectations, however.\par \par \uc2 "The good news is that the deteriorating trend has stopped, the bad news is that the deficit remains very large," said Tim Ash, emerging markets strategist at Standard Bank, in a client note.\par \par \uc2 Egyptian stocks jumped nearly 2 percent before trimming gains as voting began in a constitutional referendum which is likely to lead to a presidential bid by army chief General Abdel Fattah al-Sisi.\par \par \uc2 Egypt's stock market has soared nearly 5 percent in the past few trading sessions to their highest since May 2010.\par \par \uc2 The Ukrainian hryvnia hit its lowest in more than four years following weekend anti-government protests\par \par \uc2 Emerging sovereign debt spreads edged out by 1 basis point to 341 bps over U.S. Treasuries, with Romania planning 10- and 30-year dollar bonds, according to Thomson Reuters news service IFR.\par \par \uc2 For CENTRAL EUROPE market report, see\par \par \uc2 For TURKISH market report, see\par \par \uc2 For RUSSIAN market report, see )\par \par \uc2 MARKETS-EMERGING | C | D | E | M | O | U | MTL | GRO | SOF | OIL | RBN | GFN | Z | RNP | DNP | PTD   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020140117ea1e000hw\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
