\par\par \b \uc2 Turkish Markets Vulnerable After Fed Tapering\b0\par\par\uc2 By Yeliz Candemir   \par \uc2 558 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 19 Dezember 2013\par 11:34\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2013, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 ISTANBUL--Turkey's markets were volatile Thursday after the U.S. Federal Reserve decided to start scaling back its monthly bond purchases, a move which initially prompted a selloff in Turkish assets and forced the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  in Ankara to take action.\par \par \uc2 Turkey's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said it will sell on Dec. 23 a minimum $250 million, up from $100 million previously, as part of additional tightening to support the lira. Ankara's move followed the Fed's decision Wednesday to taper by $10 billion its bond-buying program, which had helped flood emerging markets like Turkey with cash, as the recovery in the world's largest economy gains traction.\par \par \uc2 Turkey's lira slumped by almost 1% against the dollar following the Fed decision, weakening to 2.0624 per dollar early Thursday and nearing a record low, before reversing losses to gain 0.2% after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said it would more than double its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Turkey\b0 \highlight\uc2 's benchmark two-year bond yields surged to 9.42% from 9.36% before easing to 9.25%, and Istanbul's benchmark stock index was flat at 71,357.1 at 0920 GMT, after losing nearly 2% in initial trading before recovering on the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  announcement.\par \par \uc2 Analysts warn Turkey is still in the firing line, as the Fed tapering may lead investors to start differentiating between developing economies and choke off capital inflows into some countries. Turkey is in the so-called "Fragile Five" group, with Brazil, India, South Africa and Indonesia, due to its external vulnerabilities, led by a current-account deficit at 7.5% of its $786 billion gross domestic product.\par \par \uc2 "Now, while emerging markets might be able to take this initial move to taper on the chin, individual emerging-market country fundamentals still matter--probably more so now. And therein Turkey and the lira's problem still is the current account deficit, a wide external financing gap, a \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  that is kicking and screaming to avoid narrowing the gap by hiking policy rates and slowing domestic demand," said Tim Ash, head of emerging market research at \uc2 Standard Bank PLC\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Aside from global developments such as Fed tapering, Turkey is also facing rising political risks at home that could pressure the domestic markets, analysts say. Turkish police on Tuesday detained 52 people, including the sons of three cabinet ministers and the chief executive officer of a state-owned bank, as part of a corruption investigation. The probe, which analysts say is part of a tug of war between Prime Minister Recep Tayyip Erdogan and an influential Islamic cleric, is rattling Turkey just three months before critical local elections and putting additional pressure on Turkish assets.\par \par \uc2 "This [Fed tapering] will eliminate the uncertainty for the markets and the sooner the tapering started the better for the markets in our view, despite the headwinds such as weaker lira and higher rates we may see for the short run...We think that political risks could further escalate until the elections, especially equities' performance could be highly volatile which would lead Turkey to decouple from emerging-market peers in terms of asset prices," said Tera Brokers in Istanbul.\par \par \uc2 Write to Yeliz Candemir at yeliz.candemir@wsj.com\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 December 19, 2013 05:34 ET (10:34 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020131219e9cj0016i\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
