\par\par \b \uc2 Turk lira reverses gains on Syria outlook, doubts over c.bank\b0\par\par\uc2 By Seda Sezer   \par \uc2 483 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 4 September 2013\par 17:25\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2013 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 (Recasts, updates prices, adds quote and context)\par \par \uc2 ISTANBUL, Sept 4 (Reuters) - The Turkish lira gave up some of its earlier gains on Wednesday after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  failed to reassure investors on its strategy to support the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and military strikes on neighbouring Syria moved a step closer.\par \par \uc2 Russian President \uc2 Vladimir Putin\uc2  signalled a readiness to drop his opposition to potential U.S.-led strikes on Syria if Damascus were proven to have carried out a chemical weapons attack.\par \par \uc2 Putin's comments come after U.S. President \uc2 Barack Obama\uc2  clinched the backing of key figures in Congress for his plan to punish the Syrian government with limited strikes, though no vote on that proposal is due until next week.\par \par \uc2 The lira eased to 2.0606 against the dollar by 1433 GMT, from 2.0520 earlier and not far off last week's record lows. It was also near record lows against the dollar/euro basket at 2.3873.\par \par \uc2 Financial markets have been concerned about possible U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 Turkey\b0 \highlight\uc2 's southern neighbour, thinking it could push oil prices higher in the short term, further increasing Turkey's import bill and its gaping current account deficit.\par \par \uc2 The lira hit a record low of 2.07 against the dollar on Aug. 28, around 15 percent down from its peak this year, after \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  Governor Erdem Basci ruled out interest rate hikes to defend the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 That surprise announcement left economists wondering how the bank would support the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the face of fears about an imminent tapering in U.S. stimulus, the conflict in Syria, and the current account gap.\par \par \uc2 The deficit makes Turkey particularly vulnerable to cuts in the U.S. Federal Reserve's stimulus programme because further falls in the lira would make it more expensive to finance.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  suggested at a meeting with economists on Wednesday that more surprises lay ahead in its unorthodox efforts to manage the lira, including the use of gross reserves, but investors were unconvinced.\par \par \uc2 "They seem very, very reluctant to raise rates, even in a situation with the lira going through 2.4, 2.5 ... against (the euro/dollar) basket," said Standard Bank economist Timothy Ash.\par \par \uc2 "So the mix now is basically fixed/anchored policy rates, and willingness to live with a weaker \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," he said.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has sold $8 billion at \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  auctions to support the lira so far this year.\par \par \uc2 The 10-year benchmark bond yield fell to 9.98 percent from 10.24 percent at Tuesday's close.\par \par \uc2 The main Istanbul share index fell 0.01 percent to 66,965.84 points, underperforming emerging markets peers which rose 0.25 percent. (Editing by Nick Tattersall and Stephen Nisbet)\par \par \uc2 MARKETS-TURKEY/CLOSE | ABN | D | E | RBN | GBN | GFN | M | RNP | DNP | PTD   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020130904e994000rd\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
