\par\par \b \uc2 Turkish assets firm on Syria delay,  \highlight22\uc2 central bank \highlight\uc2  eyed\b0\par\par\uc2 377 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 2 September 2013\par 11:06\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2013 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has signalled Monday could be key day\par \par \uc2 * Additional \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  may be sold at auction\par \par \uc2 * Delay to Syria \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  brings some relief\par \par \uc2 By Dasha Afanasieva\par \par \uc2 ISTANBUL, Aug 29 (Reuters) - Turkish assets firmed on Monday with a delay to possible U.S. military action in Syria bringing some relief and investors expecting further measures from the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to curb \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  volatility.\par \par \uc2 The lira firmed to 2.0160 against the dollar by 0806 GMT, from 2.0320 late on Thursday. Markets were closed on Friday for a national holiday.\par \par \uc2 The 10-year benchmark bond yield fell to 10.02 percent from 10.28 percent at Thursday's close. The main Istanbul share index rose 2.48 percent to 68,040.48 points, outperforming emerging markets peers.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  Governor Erdem Basci hinted last week that additional monetary tightening measures, including a \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  auction, to be implemented on Monday could be a template for its future policy moves.\par \par \uc2 "The tightening on Monday should be watched closely. We put it out there as an example," Basci told state-run Anadolu news agency in an interview last Tuesday ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.aafinans.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 www.aafinans.com}}}\uc2 ).\par \par \uc2 As part of the tightening, the bank is not holding a one-week repo auction and will hold a minimum $100 million \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  auction to give the lira additional support.\par \par \uc2 Economists interpreted Basci's comments as meaning the bank could increase the volume of its \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  auctions.\par \par \uc2 "As he stressed the extensive \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves at the bank's disposal there is a high likelihood of even more aggressive \b \highlight22\uc2 forex intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  today," \uc2 Commerzbank\uc2  analysts said in a note.\par \par \uc2 Markets were pricing out the risk of an immediate military \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in Syria after U.S. President Barack Obama said that he would not attack Syria before seeking approval from Congress, which reconvenes on Sept. 9.\par \par \uc2 Financial markets have been concerned about possible U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 Turkey\b0 \highlight\uc2 's southern neighbour, fearing it could push oil prices higher in the short term, further increasing Turkey's import bill and its gaping current account deficit. (Reporting by Dasha Afanasieva and Ece Toksabay; Editing by Nick Tattersall and Susan Fenton)\par \par \uc2 MARKETS-TURKEY/ | ABN | D | E | RBN | GBN | GFN | M | RNP | DNP | PTD   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020130902e992000f8\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
