\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 3-\uc2 Turkish  \highlight22\uc2 central bank \highlight\uc2  says won't defend lira with interest rates\b0\par\par\uc2 971 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 27 August 2013\par 16:03\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2013 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * Basci all but rules out interest rate hike\par \par \uc2 * Lira hits record low, bond yields jump, stocks slide\par \par \uc2 * U.S. Fed, Syria, elections weigh on Turkish appeal\par \par \uc2 * Lira slide hits corporate earnings (Adds analyst comment, updates market reaction)\par \par \uc2 By Seda Sezer and Nick Tattersall\par \par \uc2 ISTANBUL, Aug 27 (Reuters) - Turkish \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  Governor Erdem Basci said on Tuesday he did not intend to hike interest rates to defend a sliding lira, which hit record lows on concern about the outlook for U.S. stimulus and the conflict in neighbouring Syria.\par \par \uc2 In an interview with the state-run Anadolu news agency (AA), Basci said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had $40 billion in reserves which it could use to shore up the lira and would \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  defensively as needed to reduce exchange rate volatility.\par \par \uc2 The lira weakened to a record low of 2.037 to the dollar as markets wondered whether the bank had the firepower necessary to defend the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The main Turkish share index slid 4.7 percent to close at its lowest in a year.\par \par \uc2 The 10-year benchmark bond yield spiked to 10.83 percent during Basci's interview, which was broadcast live on Turkish financial TV stations, from 10.18 percent on Monday. It closed at 10.28 percent.\par \par \uc2 "We will not be using our interest rate weapon against the exchange rate. We are very clear on that and we have said there will not be any uncertainty about interest rates," Basci told AA Finans ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.aafinans.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 www.aafinans.com}}}\uc2 ).\par \par \uc2 "Since we will not be using this then we are left with the balance sheet weapon, and that is a very powerful weapon. That means we will use our \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves against the slide in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market."\par \par \uc2 His comments surprised many economists.\par \par \uc2 "\uc2 Turkey's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is digging itself into a deeper hole. For a country whose \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves barely cover its short-term external debts, this is highly imprudent policymaking," said Nicholas Spiro of Spiro Sovereign Strategy.\par \par \uc2 Emerging markets have borne the brunt of heavy selling in recent weeks amid concern that the U.S. Federal Reserve will soon start reducing its massive bond-buying programme, which had flooded developing economies with cheap liquidity.\par \par \uc2 Turkey is particularly vulnerable because it is heavily dependent on foreign inflows to finance its current account deficit, running at over 7 percent of national output.\par \par \uc2 Concern about the consequences of a possible U.S.-led \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in neighbouring Syria and political uncertainty ahead of an election cycle beginning next year have further dampened its appeal as investors shun riskier assets.\par \par \uc2 Basci said he was not overly worried about the exchange rate, forecasting it would recover by the end of the year to around 1.92 to the dollar, and that long-term bond yields would also be back in single digits.\par \par \uc2 "Don't expect a shock from us on the interest rate side, just expect interesting manoeuvres on the \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  side that will result in an appreciation of the lira," Basci said, in characteristically cryptic comments.\par \par \uc2 "I am neither a hawk nor a dove," he said when questioned about his policy stance. "I am not a bird."\par \par \uc2 WEAK LIRA TAKES TOLL\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  raised its overnight lending rate, the upper end of the interest rate corridor it uses to control monetary conditions, for a second straight month last week, hiking it by 50 basis points to 7.75 percent in a surprise move to try to prevent an uncontrolled slide in the lira.\par \par \uc2 Basci said the average cost of lira funding would remain between 6.75 percent, the rate at which it funds primary dealers, and 7.75 percent until inflation drops to its year-end forecast of 6.2 percent.\par \par \uc2 "The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is once again demonstrating it is unwilling to raise rates much further, and that will continue to drag (the dollar/lira rate) higher," Luis Costa, head of CEEMEA \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and debt strategy at Citi, referring to more lira weakening.\par \par \uc2 Economy Minister Zafer Caglayan, a vocal supporter of low interest rates and champion of Turkish exporters, who benefit from a weak lira, said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  did not need to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , saying the 2 to the dollar level it breached on Tuesday was only a psychological barrier.\par \par \uc2 He also dismissed suggestions that any Turkish participation in an international coalition to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in Syria would have a negative impact on the economy.\par \par \uc2 But the effects of the weak lira - which has fallen 14 percent against the dollar from a peak this year of 1.7455 on Feb. 1 - are already being felt by some of Turkey's top firms.\par \par \uc2 A weak lira cut net profit at national flag carrier \uc2 Turkish Airlines\uc2  by almost a third in the second quarter despite a sharp rise in sales, sending its shares tumbling more than 2 percent on Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 The country's largest telecoms group \uc2 Turk Telekom\uc2  , whose liabilities are in dollars, euros and Japanese yen, said last month its net profit fall 56 percent in the same period due to \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  losses.\par \par \uc2 The weakening lira and Basci's comments helped knock the main Istanbul share index down by more than 3 percent to a year low although it later recovered somewhat to trade down 2.4 percent by 1030 GMT.\par \par \uc2 "Combined with the uncertainty over a multi-party military \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in Syria, the comments are negative for \b \highlight22\uc2 Turkey\b0 \highlight\uc2 's financial markets," said Ibrahim Aksoy, economist at Istanbul-based Seker Securities. (Additional reporting by Daren Butler, Dasha Afanasieva, Humeyra Pamuk and Asli Kandemir; Writing by Nick Tattersall; Editing by Hugh Lawson)\par \par \uc2 TURKEY-CENTRALBANK/ (UPDATE 3) | ABN | D | E | RBN | GFN | M | ABX | BNX | FUN | AFA | CSA | LBY | RWSA | RWS | REULB | GNS | RNP | DNP | PTD   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020130827e98r0009v\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
