\par\par \b \uc2 Syria Roils  \highlight22\uc2 Foreign-Exchange \highlight\uc2  Markets\b0\par\par\uc2 1,047 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 27 August 2013\par 13:32\par \uc2 Dow Jones Global News Select\par \uc2 DJON\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2013 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 --Lira, rupee plunge to new record lows against the dollar\par \par \uc2 --Market participants seek safety in Swiss franc, yen\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par    By Clare Connaghan \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Turkish lira and Indian rupee remained under intense selling pressure Tuesday as fears of possible U.S. \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in Syria ramped up the pressure on these \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and drove traders into perceived safe retreats in times of stress, such as the yen and Swiss franc.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The lira and rupee--two \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  that have already been hit hard in the past few weeks due to concerns over how their economies will cope when the U.S. Federal Reserve starts winding down stimulus measures--slumped to new record lows against the dollar Tuesday as political tensions between Syria and the U.S. escalated.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Israeli shekel also came under pressure, falling to a near seven-week low against the dollar, after U.S. Secretary of State John Kerry said the U.S. and its allies are considering military strikes on Syria after "undeniable" evidence of a chemical attack.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "\f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Foreign-exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  markets have reacted further overnight to fears of military \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in Syria," said Elsa Lignos, senior \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  strategist at \f28 \uc2 \f2 RBC Capital Markets\f28 \uc2 \f2  in London.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Across financial markets, the crisis in Syria weighed with stock markets in Europe and the Middle East tumbling, while yields on U.S. 10-year Treasury bonds fell to their lowest level since mid-August.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 For the lira, additional pressure came from the stance of Turkish \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Governor Erdem Basci, who ruled out raising core interest rates to defend the bruised \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . In response, the lira weakened by more than 1% against the dollar which surged to a new record high of TRY2.0339. The euro also broke new ground, rising to TRY2.7163 against the lira, as the governor failed to calm market nerves.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "Basci rules out further overnight lending rate hikes, which is negative for the lira in our view given the Fed uncertainty," says Ibrahim Aksoy, an economist with Istanbul-based brokerage Seker Invest.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Fed is preparing to wind down policies that flooded financial markets with cheap cash, which is raising concerns about how countries such as Turkey, which relied on these inflows to pay for imports and finance debt, will cope without it. As a result, investors have been selling the lira aggressively and so far this month, the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  is down more than 3% against the dollar.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Turkey's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has increased sales of dollars to support the lira, but ultimately this measure will only dampen depreciation, not reverse it, says Thu Lan Nguyen, a \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  strategist at \f28 \uc2 \f2 Commerzbank\f28 \uc2 \f2 .\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "If markets are in a risk off mode there is hardly anything you can do as a \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 ," says Ms Nguyen.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The situation is the same for India, where the rupee sunk to new life-time low against the dollar Tuesday of INR66.07 despite the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank intervening\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , according to local dealers. India, which like \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Turkey\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has seen its \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  swoon in anticipation of a shift in Fed policy, also faces the extra burden of higher oil prices, which are also climbing amid the Syrian tensions.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Caught up in the emerging-markets tension, the South African rand sank close to a four-year low against the dollar, which hit ZAR10.4394.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 In other news, data showing business sentiment in the euro-zone's largest economy--Germany--leapt in August amid an improving export outlook, had limited impact on the euro which remained weaker against the dollar on the day.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Looking ahead, aside from watching the situation in Syria, Case Shiller house prices and consumer confidence data are due for release at 1300 GMT and 1400 GMT respectively.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "The market is digesting the weak durable good orders we had from the U.S. yesterday which has put uncertainty back on the agenda leading up to the FOMC meeting," said Michael Sneyd, a \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign-exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  strategist at \f28 \uc2 \f2 BNP Paribas\f28 \uc2 \f2  in London.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Data showed total orders for durable goods such as cars and furniture dropped 7.3% in July after three months of gains, worse than economists had predicted. The weak report complicates the outlook for Federal Reserve policy, as Fed members are debating whether the U.S. economy is healthy enough to begin winding down its post-crisis stimulus measures as early as next month.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Against this backdrop, price action is likely to remain choppy with investors not really wanting to commit to new trades, Mr Sneyd added.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 At 1101 GMT, the euro was trading at $1.3346 against the dollar, compared with $1.3370 late Monday in New York, according to trading system EBS. The dollar was at Y97.80 against the yen, compared with Y98.50, while the euro was at Y130.525, compared with Y131.72. The pound was trading at $1.5515 against the dollar, compared with $1.5573 late Monday in New York.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Wall Street Journal Dollar Index, which tracks the U.S. dollar against a basket of major \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , was at 73.87 from 73.844.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 A summary of key levels for chart-watching technical strategists is below:\f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  spot:       EUR/USD    USD/JPY    GBP/USD    USD/CHF \par  \par Spot 1039 GMT     1.3345     97.78      1.5514     0.9215 \par 3 Day Trend       Range      Bearish    Bearish    Range \par Weekly Trend      Bullish    Range      Bullish    Bearish \par 200 day ma        1.3109     94.45      1.5478     0.9370 \par 3rd Resistance    1.3394     98.75      1.5639     0.9290 \par 2nd Resistance    1.3375     98.40      1.5611     0.9263 \par 1st Resistance    1.3354     98.04      1.5560     0.9246 \par Pivot*            1.3373     98.51      1.5581     0.9228 \par 1st Support       1.3322     97.65      1.5500     0.9182 \par 2nd Support       1.3298     97.40      1.5475     0.9146 \par 3rd Support       1.3255     96.91      1.5424     0.9129 \par  \par  \par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  spot:       EUR/GBP \par  \par Spot 1039 GMT     0.8604 \par 3 Day Trend       Bullish \par Weekly Trend      Bearish \par 200 day ma        0.8472 \par 3rd Resistance    0.8680 \par 2nd Resistance    0.8635 \par 1st Resistance    0.8616 \par Pivot*            0.8586 \par 1st Support       0.8582 \par 2nd Support 