\par\par \b \uc2 DJ Turkish Lira Sinks as  \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank \highlight\uc2  Rules Out Further Rate Hikes\b0\par\par\uc2 By Yeliz Candemir and Clare Connaghan   \par \uc2 391 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 27 August 2013\par 11:34\par \uc2 Dow Jones Chinese Newswires English Content\par \uc2 RTNW\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2013, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 ISTANBUL--The Turkish lira slumped to yet another record low against the euro and dollar Tuesday as the country's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor rules out further rate hikes.\par \par \uc2 The lira weakened over 1% against both the dollar and euro following the governor's speech. The dollar surged past TRY2.03 against the lira for the first time ever, while the euro rose to a new record high of TRY2.7163.\par \par \uc2 By 0810 GMT, the dollar was trading at TRY2.0285, up from TRY2.0050 before the governor's speech. The euro was trading at TRY2.7055, up from around TRY2.68 before the speech started.\par \par \uc2 In an interview with state-run news agency Anadolu Agency, Mr. Basci said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will fund the market at 6.75% until the inflation rate falls to the 6.2% from the current 8.8% by the end of this year. He said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will fund the market at 7.75% on additional tightening days, but he said the cost of funding for the banks won't be more expensive than the 7.75% rate. He said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will use \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves to defend the lira, but won't use interest rates to stem the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's slide.\par \par \uc2 "USD/TRY will be 1.92 by the year end and don't be surprised when you see that level," Mr. Basci said. He said markets shouldn't expect interest rate hikes but should expect rates to remain steady.\par \par \uc2 "Basci rules out further overnight lending rate hikes, which is negative for the lira in our view given the Fed uncertainty. The \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  Governor has also said that the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  movements may be rapid, but the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  would likely gain value once again should the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  be successful in controlling short-term interest rates," said Ibrahim Aksoy, an economist with Istanbul-based brokerage Seker Invest. "Overall, the comments so far are negative for the lira, bond and equity markets," Mr. Aksoy said, combined with the uncertainty over a possible U.S. military \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in Syria, the comments are negative for \b \highlight22\uc2 Turkey\b0 \highlight\uc2 's financial markets.\par \par \uc2 Write to Yeliz Candemir at yeliz.candemir@dowjones.com\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 27-08-13 0934GMT\par \par \uc2 Dokument RTNW000020130827e98r000bx\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
