\par\par \b \uc2 Mexican Peso, Emerging-Market  \highlight22\uc2 Currencies \highlight\uc2  Slip on Fed Worries\b0\par\par\uc2 By Erin McCarthy   \par \uc2 564 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 26 August 2013\par 22:29\par \uc2 Dow Jones Global Equities News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2013 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 The Mexican peso and most other emerging-market \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  slumped Monday, resuming the selloff that has plagued them in recent weeks.\par \par \uc2 Investors returned their focus to the Federal Reserve's September policy meeting, where the Fed could start to trim its bond-buying stimulus program that had sent investors on a hunt for yield in past years. The threat of less Fed stimulus has rapidly tamped investors' enthusiasm for higher-yielding emerging-market assets, and has caused many to reinvest in U.S. assets.\par \par \uc2 Several emerging-market \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  recovered slightly on Friday in the wake of larger \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  efforts on the part of Brazil's and \b \highlight22\uc2 Turkey\b0 \highlight\uc2 's central banks over the course of the week. However, these \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  once again took on a bearish tone Monday, with little sign of such \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  having an effect as Brazil's and \b \highlight22\uc2 Turkey\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  weakened.\par \par \uc2 "September's getting closer and closer," said Win Thin, global head of emerging-market \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategy at \uc2 Brown Brothers Harriman\uc2  in New York. "It's pretty much a full-scale emerging-market selloff continued."\par \par \uc2 Mexico's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  led the way, diving 1.8% against the dollar, which bought MXN13.1827, according to CQG. The peso often acts as a proxy for emerging-market \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , since it is one of the more heavily traded and accessible \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the asset class.\par \par \uc2 Brazil's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  also weakened sharply, despite the \uc2 Brazilian \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's heightened efforts to stop the real's seeming one-way decline last week. \uc2 Brazil's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Thursday said it would provide at least $60 billion more in dollar liquidity through the end of the year. Under the plan, the bank will offer $3 billion of dollar loans and swaps per week in regular auctions starting Friday. Still, the real fell 1.4% against the dollar, which bought BRL2.3813 late Monday.\par \par \uc2 In Asia, the rupee weakened, though India's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was suspected of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market toward the close of local trading Monday. The rupee slid 1% against the greenback, which traded at INR64.32, according to CQG.\par \par \uc2 The rupee and Brazilian real have been severely punished by traders this month as their countries have large current account deficits. These current account gaps force them to rely on foreign portfolio inflows to meet financing needs, but these flows could lessen if the Fed pulls back stimulus, analysts say.\par \par \uc2 The Indonesian rupiah, however, saw some recovery in response to a group of measures the government announced last week aimed at narrowing the country's current account gap. \uc2 Indonesia's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  announced additional measures Friday aimed at stabilizing local markets and the economy as well.\par \par \uc2 The rupiah fell 1.7% to IDR10,845 against the dollar.\par \par \uc2 "The measures from both the government and \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  are certainly well-intentioned and a step in the right direction,' said \uc2 HSBC\uc2  ASEAN economist \uc2 Su Sian LIM\uc2  in a note Monday.\par \par \uc2 In Europe, the Turkish lira underperformed, despite continued \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by \b \highlight22\uc2 Turkey\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which sold $350 million in \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support the lira Monday. After hovering near record lows earlier in the session, the lira slipped 0.5% against the dollar, which bought TRY1.9982, according to CQG.\par \par \uc2 Write to Erin McCarthy at erin.mccarthy@wsj.com [ 26-08-13 2029GMT ]\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020130826e98q000e1\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
