\par\par \b \uc2 Indian Rupee Defies Broader Emerging-Market  \highlight22\uc2 Currency \highlight\uc2  Slump\b0\par\par\uc2 By Erin McCarthy  \par \uc2 572 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 24 Juli 2013\par 18:43\par \uc2 Dow Jones Global Equities News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2013 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 The Indian rupee surged against the dollar Wednesday on the back of the \uc2 Reserve Bank of India\uc2 's latest efforts to shore up the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , while most other emerging-market \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  fell.\par \par \uc2 The rupee soared more than 1% to a one-week high against the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which recently bought INR59.12.\par \par \uc2 The RBI late Tuesday put new restrictions on commercial banks' access to cash. Banks now are permitted to borrow cash up to only 0.5% of their net deposits from the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  daily at 7.25%, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said in a news release posted on its website. It also said banks must set aside more cash with it than they did before.\par \par \uc2 These measures are only the latest in a series of steps to prop up the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which has been pummeled by concerns about the Federal Reserve withdrawing its stimulus that had helped drive investors to higher-yielding assets.\par \par \uc2 While these latest measures helped drive the rupee higher, they actually dragged down India's local bond and equity markets and raised concerns that further liquidity-tightening could hit these markets even harder.\par \par \uc2 "We do think it's going to stem the short-term pressure on the rupee," said \uc2 Ilan Solot\uc2 , emerging-market \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at \uc2 Brown Brothers Harriman\uc2 . But he warned that additional tightening could cause "collateral damage" in other markets and spook away much-needed short-term equity flows.\par \par \uc2 Other emerging-market \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , however, broadly weakened on the back of disappointing Chinese economic data and positive U.S. housing data. \uc2 HSBC\uc2 's Chinese manufacturing Purchasing Managers' Index dropped to an 11-month low at 47.7 in July, from 48.2 in June.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, U.S. new-home sales surged 8.3% in June, renewing worries that the Fed could start tapering its bond-buying stimulus if the economic outlook improves in the world's largest economy.\par \par \uc2 The Brazilian real suffered the largest slide against the dollar, despite \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by \uc2 Brazil's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  held a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  swap auction Wednesday aimed at supporting the real, which slumped more than 1% against the dollar. The U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  bought BRL2.2433 from BRL2.2133 late Tuesday, according to CQG.\par \par \uc2 The Mexican peso also slid significantly as a rise in U.S. Treasurys lent support to the dollar. The peso slumped 1.2% against the dollar, which traded at MXN12.6485.\par \par \uc2 The Turkish lira was the top decliner among emerging European \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , despite the recent rate hike by its \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  and continued market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . On Tuesday, \b \highlight22\uc2 Turkey\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  raised its overnight lending rate by 0.75 percentage point to 7.25% and signaled that it could tighten further, in an attempt to halt the lira's relentless decline. But that, along with \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  selling auctions Wednesday, wasn't enough to halt the lira's dive. The lira weakened 1% against the dollar, which changed hands at TRY1.9194, according to CQG.\par \par \uc2 The South African rand slid as well, despite better-than-expected inflation data. It fell 0.6% against the dollar, which bought ZAR9.7377. The annual inflation rate ticked down to 5.5% from 5.6% in May, according to South Africa's statistics agency.\par \par \uc2 --Khushita Vasant and Ashutosh Joshi contributed to this article.\par \par \uc2 Write to Erin McCarthy at erin.mccarthy@wsj.com [ 24-07-13 1643GMT ]\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020130724e97o000mx\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
