\par\par \b \uc2 DJ Turkey Expected to Raise Rates Tuesday to Stem Lira's Decline\b0\par\par\uc2 By Yeliz Candemir \par \uc2 515 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 22 Juli 2013\par 15:56\par \uc2 Dow Jones Chinese Newswires English Content\par \uc2 RTNW\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2013, Dow Jones & Company, Inc. \par \par \uc2 ISTANBUL--Turkey is expected Tuesday to join a number of emerging economies, such as Brazil, India and Indonesia, with a rise in interest rates in an effort to support the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , but economists are split on the extent of the expected increase, with forecasts ranging from 50 to 100 basis points.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has spent billions of dollars in \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  and auctions in an effort to stem the lira's slide but with little effect. The bank is now considering a rate increase--its first since October 2011--to prop up the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The lira has plummeted about 8% since the beginning of this year and hit record lows against the dollar, largely as a result of a broader sell-off in emerging markets in the spring, fueled by fears that the Federal Reserve would soon start scaling back its monthly bond-buying program. Widespread clashes between police and anti-government protesters in June also weighed on the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 At 1145 GMT Monday, the lira was steady against the dollar at TRY1.9169.\par \par \uc2 A poll of ten economists by Dow Jones Newswires showed that half expect \uc2 Turkey's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to raise its 6.50% overnight lending rate by 50 basis points, while the other half expect an increase of 100 basis points, when its Monetary Policy Committee meets Tuesday. All ten expect the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to keep its overnight borrowing rate at 3.50% and one-week benchmark rate at 4.50%.\par \par \uc2 "I think the benchmark for the market will be the 100 bps move point--less than this and Turkish assets are likely to come under renewed selling pressure, more than this and they are likely to rally as the market will assume that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is finally looking to get ahead (or rather "on") of the curve in terms of required tightening," said Tim Ash, head of emerging markets research at \uc2 Standard Bank PLC\uc2  in London.\par \par \uc2 Last week, \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  Governor Erdem Basci said policy makers would consider "a measured step to widen the interest-rate corridor" that ranges from 3.5% to 6.5% at its regular monthly meeting July 23. The corridor allows policy makers to vary borrowing costs daily in an effort to meet targets ranging from economic growth to financial stability.\par \par \uc2 "If a move of 50 basis points or less is announced, we expect TRY [the lira] to sell off very sharply with USD/TRY highly likely to breach the 2.00 handle. However, the risk of this is too great and given that \b \highlight22\uc2 forex intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  has proven ineffective and \b \highlight22\uc2 Turkey\b0 \highlight\uc2 's foreign reserves are very limited, the bank has little choice," said Christian Lawrence, emerging market strategist at \uc2 Rabobank\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has spent more than 10% of its net \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves in market \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 , and has sold $6.6 billion in \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  auctions, since June 11.\par \par \uc2 Write to Yeliz Candemir at yeliz.candemir@dowjones.com\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 22-07-13 1356GMT\par \par \uc2 Dokument RTNW000020130722e97