\par\par \b \uc2 DJ Performance of Emerging-Market  \highlight22\uc2 Currencies \highlight\uc2  Improves as Dollar Weakens\b0\par\par\uc2 By Prabha Natarajan   \par \uc2 553 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 22 Juli 2013\par 19:18\par \uc2 Dow Jones Newswires\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright (c) 2013, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 The pro-growth focus of the \uc2 Group of 20\uc2  countries over the weekend has given investors confidence and prompted a recovery of most emerging-market \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  against the dollar on Monday.\par \par \uc2 The Turkish lira gained 0.3% on the day, according to CQG data, on a combination of improved global outlook and expectations of a rate increase in Turkey.\par \par \uc2 In addition to the G-20 conclusion, Japanese Prime Minister Shinzo Abe's party saw a strong showing in parliamentary elections which also served as a referendum to his administration's reforms and weakening of the yen.\par \par \uc2 This set off a weakness in the dollar that has lingered through the New York trading session.\par \par \uc2 Additionally, in Turkey, analysts expect the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  there to raise its overnight lending rate by as much as 100 basis points at its monetary policy meeting on Tuesday, in a bid to support the weakening lira.\par \par \uc2 "We believe the bank is more likely to deliver a moderately hawkish surprise," \uc2 Goldman Sachs\uc2  analysts said in a note.\par \par \uc2 Standard Chartered analysts note that the recent protests have exposed Turkey's vulnerabilities to investors, and at the same time diminished its policy options.\par \par \uc2 Investors who previously had held Turkish bonds have sharply lowered their exposure as a result and this has resulted in a selloff in all Turkish assets, especially the lira. Though \b \highlight22\uc2 Turkey\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  regularly to defend the lira, much of the recent retracement in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's value was due to the expectation of rate increases. Some analysts, though, worry that such a move would pressure Turkey's growth, which already is sluggish due to the recession in most of Europe.\par \par \uc2 Also, in anticipation of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  action, Hungary's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  continued to gain. It recently traded at 294.11 forints, up 0.5% on the day to the euro. In recent weeks, investors have been drawn to Hungarian assets drawn by the resilience of these assets at a time when other emerging-market assets were tumbling lower. Also, \uc2 Hungary's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is expected to continue easing, with analysts projecting a 25 basis-point cut to its key policy rate to 4%, in a bid to support growth at a time when inflation is low.\par \par \uc2 Even at the 4%, investors say Hungary is an attractive carry play as its yield is higher than comparable European peers.\par \par \uc2 In Latin America, the Brazilian \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor's comments that the bank would focus only on fighting inflation, has raised expectations of more rate increases in the coming months. The dollar fell 0.64% during the day to 2.2325 Brazilian reais after another round of \b \highlight22\uc2 central-bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  auctions to strengthen the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, the South African rand's retracement in recent sessions has prompted Bernd Berg, global emerging-markets strategist at \uc2 Credit Suisse\uc2 , to recommend buying the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  versus the dollar. He expects the rand to improve from improved external factors, capital inflows and the attraction of higher rates to carry-trade focused investors.\par \par \uc2 Recently, the dollar traded 0.65% lower to the rand at ZAR9.8067, according to CQG data.\par \par \uc2 Write to Prabha Natarajan at prabha.natarajan@dowjones.com\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 July 22, 2013 13:18 ET (17:18 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020130722e97m003tp\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
