\par\par \b \uc2 CORRECTED- \highlight22\uc2 Central bank \highlight\uc2  reserves perilously low in some developing countries\b0\par\par\uc2 By Sujata Rao   \par \uc2 578 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 Juli 2013\par 16:00\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2013 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 (Corrects Chinese reserves figure to over $3 trillion)\par \par \uc2 LONDON, July 18 (Reuters) - Severely depleted \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves are putting Ukraine, Egypt and Venezuela at risk of balance of payments crises while reserves in many other developing countries are also steadily declining.\par \par \uc2 Based on a comparison of monthly import needs and maturing short-term debt, most emerging economies - with a few exceptions - still have ample reserves, as the following graphic, based on \uc2 Bank of America\uc2 Merrill Lynch\uc2  data, shows:\par \par \uc2 For a graphic, click on: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://link.reuters.com/sef79t"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://link.reuters.com/sef79t}}}\par \par \uc2 One yardstick of reserve adequacy is the number of months of imports the reserves will buy, with three months deemed to be the safe minimum. The second, based on the so-called Guidotti-Greenspan rule, requires reserves to be at least equal to external debt payments due in the coming year.\par \par \uc2 The rationale is that countries should have enough reserves to resist a sudden stop in foreign financing.\par \par \uc2 By the first measure, Egypt and Venezuela, with less than two months apiece of import cover, and Ukraine, with three months, look most vulnerable. Ukraine's reserves are also insufficient to cover debt maturing before mid-2014.\par \par \uc2 Another possible weak link is Turkey, which on the face of it has five months' import cover and a reserves-to-short-term debt ratio of 1. But Turkey's net usable reserves are actually far lower, with \uc2 HSBC\uc2  estimating the figure as low as $40 billion, giving import cover of just 2.3 months.\par \par \uc2 David Hauner\uc2 , head of EEMEA debt strategy at BofA \uc2 Merrill Lynch\uc2  says Turkey also looks vulnerable by the other measure, of maturing foreign debt.\par \par \uc2 "Turkey ... barely covers the one-year period. That is why people get so nervous when \b \highlight22\uc2 Turkey intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market and that is why you are seeing such a huge underperformance of Turkish assets in the external debt market," Hauner said.\par \par \uc2 "But among big emerging markets very few are running a ratio of less than 2. Clearly they have raised the bar on themselves."\par \par \uc2 Emerging markets hold the lion's share of central banks' combined $11.1 trillion reserves, recent IMF data shows - a legacy of the past decade's trade and investment boom. Over $3 trillion of this is in China.\par \par \uc2 But as exports and capital inflows slow, accumulation has stalled and is even reversing as central banks from Brazil to Poland are forced to sell dollars to support falling \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 It is unclear exactly how much emerging central banks have spent on \b \highlight22\uc2 currency interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  since the sell-off started in May but they range from Brazil's sale of $20 billion in derivatives to $6.2 billion in Turkey and $5 billion in Russia.\par \par \uc2 Reserves have therefore fallen since the figures above were compiled. Latest data shows Indonesia's stash at $98.1 billion, down $9 billion over May-June, while India now has $280.1 billion compared to $296 billion in early May.\par \par \uc2 Some of the moves reflect valuation effects such as exchange rate changes and a lower gold price. But further falls could send more countries into risky territory. India and South Africa both of which have 4.5-5 months' import cover, reserve/debt ratios of 2 or less and large current account gaps, look especially vulnerable. (Graphic by Vincent Flasseur; Editing by Catherine Evans)\par \par \uc2 EMERGING-RESERVES (CORRECTED) | GFN | SF | ABN | M | D | Z | DNP   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020130718e97i000rb\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
