\par\par \b \uc2 DJ Brazilian Real Turns Volatile as More Rate Hikes Are Projected\b0\par\par\uc2 By Prabha Natarajan   \par \uc2 598 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 Juli 2013\par 16:47\par \uc2 Dow Jones Newswires\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright (c) 2013, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 The Brazilian real see-sawed on Thursday as it moved from strength to weakness and back as investors' digested the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's latest take on the country's economic health.\par \par \uc2 The real recently traded at BRL2.2206, a gain of 0.2% on the day to the dollar, according to CQG data.\par \par \uc2 Market participants were surprised at the hawkish message from the minutes of \uc2 Brazil's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's recent meeting released Thursday. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  acknowledged that the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's sharp fall in recent weeks added to rising inflation but suggests the resulting adjustments to prices is good for the economy, said Tony Volpon, head of emerging-market research Americas at \uc2 Nomura Securities International Inc\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Further, the minutes suggested Brazil would continue to tighten monetary policy. It already has raised key policy rates by 100 basis points.\par \par \uc2 In minutes released Thursday of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's July 10 decision, policy makers said weakness in the Brazilian real versus the dollar "constitutes a strong source of shorter-term inflationary pressure." However, the longer-term effects of a weaker real can be limited through "adequate" monetary policy measures, the bank said.\par \par \uc2 These comments have prompted Citi analyst Marcelo Kfoury to suggest Brazil would raise rates to 9.25% in the current cycle.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, an auction of \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  swap contracts on Thursday helped the real strengthen against the dollar.\par \par \uc2 In other \b \highlight22\uc2 central-bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  actions, the South African \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  kept its key policy rates unchanged at 5%. The bank's governor said slower growth is making the bank more tolerant to inflation, which is heading close to its comfort level of 6%.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, the bank once again reduced its growth forecast for the year to 2% from its previous estimate of 2.4%, and to 3.3% from 3.5%% for 2014.\par \par \uc2 South Africa's growth has stumbled after last year's mining strikes that have triggered labor unrest and extended labor negotiations. Also, the fall in commodity prices has hurt the exporter of precious metals.\par \par \uc2 The dollar rose 0.5% to the South African rand to ZAR9.8774, according to CQG data.\par \par \uc2 In \b \highlight22\uc2 Turkey\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  continued to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in an attempt to reduce volatility in the lira. The dollar rose 0.44% to TRY1.92, according to CQG data.\par \par \uc2 Market participants believe despite the day's weakness, emerging-market \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  will be supported in coming weeks as investors take advantage of these lower levels. Already, many investors have said they have bought local bonds of Mexico and Brazil.\par \par \uc2 In Mexico, the peso has rebounded below MXN12.4558, for the first time in more than seven weeks, according to CQG data. Investors cite the administration's renewed focus on reforms and the country's close ties to an improved U.S. economy.\par \par \uc2 In the debt markets, some emerging-market issuers tiptoed back in, including Asia's first high-yield deal since June. PT Multipolar TK of Indonesia is in the market with a $200 million, five-year note that has a guidance in the area of 9.875% yield.\par \par \uc2 Other issuers include Russian Agricultural bank and \uc2 Banco do Brasil\uc2 . The Russian bank is selling a $500 million bond that has a guidance of 5.4% yield. \uc2 Banco do Brasil\uc2  expects to sell a EUR500 million, five-year bond at a yield of 4%.\par \par \uc2 --Paulo Trevisani contributed to this article.\par \par \uc2 Write to Prabha Natarajan at prabha.natarajan@dowjones.com\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 July 18, 2013 10:47 ET (14:47 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020130718e97i003qa\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
