\par\par \b \uc2 DJ Brazilian Real, Turkish Lira Lead Emerging  \highlight22\uc2 Currencies \highlight\uc2 ' Decline\b0\par\par\uc2 By Prabha Natarajan   \par \uc2 396 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 12 Juli 2013\par 21:10\par \uc2 Dow Jones Newswires\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright (c) 2013, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 Emerging-market \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  and central banks were little match for the stronger dollar Friday.\par \par \uc2 Despite \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 , \b \highlight22\uc2 Turkey\b0 \highlight\uc2 's lira fell to TRY1.9580, down 0.35% on the day, according to CQG data.\par \par \uc2 Many investors have completely cashed out of their Turkey holdings, especially in recent weeks after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  began its \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 "\b \highlight22\uc2 Turkey\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been disappointing," said Richard House, head of emerging-market debt at \uc2 Standard Life Investments\uc2 , with $272.6 billion in assets under management.\par \par \uc2 His fund had the highest exposure to the lira and lira-denominated assets, but he began selling after they saw the government's response to protestors back in May. Since then, his fund has been slowly selling to its current position of zero exposure to the country.\par \par \uc2 Increasingly, market participants have begun to think that Turkey is ill-using its reserves by trying to keep up an exchange rate in the name of \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  stability. The country's widening current-account deficit and slowing growth also are other reasons for investors to keep their distance.\par \par \uc2 On Friday, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was once more in the market to protect the lira after the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  jumped above TRY1.96 to the dollar.\par \par \uc2 Brazil's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  weakened after the country's monthly activity indicator showed a weaker outcome in May, which prompted Citi to reduce its growth forecast to 2.2% for 2013 from 2.5%. The real recently was 0.56% weaker to the dollar at BRL2.2697, according to CQG data.\par \par \uc2 In Mexico, an unexpectedly dovish statement from \uc2 Mexico's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  created a flutter in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market. Many investors who hold its government's long bonds are reading it as a sign that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  may cut rates in the future. It's unclear if this would happen, said Eduardo Suarez, strategist at Scotiabank.\par \par \uc2 But if the Mexico were to cut key policy rates below 4%, it would be a positive for investors. Lower bond rates could push up prices and these long-term holders could benefit, he said.\par \par \uc2 The dollar gained against the peso to MXN12.8258, after falling a bit after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  statement, according to CQG data.\par \par \uc2 Write to Prabha Natarajan at prabha.natarajan@dowjones.com\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 July 12, 2013 15:10 ET (19:10 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020130712e97c00500\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
