\par\par \b \uc2 EMERGING MARKETS-Stocks eye positive week, lira eases\b0\par\par\uc2 411 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 12 Juli 2013\par 12:03\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2013 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 LONDON, July 12 (Reuters) - Emerging stocks were heading for a rare week of gains on Friday, buoyed by hopes the Fed would not turn off the liquidity taps any time soon, while \b \highlight22\uc2 Turkey\b0 \highlight\uc2 's lira edged towards record lows despite recent \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Attempts by U.S. Federal Chairman \uc2 Ben Bernanke\uc2  this week to row back on previous comments about the tapering of the Fed's money-printing programme have given support to high-yielding emerging markets.\par \par \uc2 The MSCI emerging stocks index has risen 2.7 percent this week though it remains 11 percent down from May 22, the date of Bernanke's initial remarks about tapering.\par \par \uc2 The index was steady on Friday after soaring 3 percent in the previous session, its largest one-day gain since Sept 2012. Russian stocks  rose more than 1 percent to hit their highest in over a month, South African stocks hit three-week highs and Turkish stocks rose 0.3 percent.\par \par \uc2 Chinese shares  fell, however, ahead of GDP data due on Monday.\par \par \uc2 China's finance minister signalled that Beijing may be willing to tolerate second half economic growth significantly below 7 percent, the most sobering comment to date on the country's slowdown from a senior policymaker.\par \par \uc2 Emerging sovereign debt spreads inched out 1 basis point to 358 bps over U.S. Treasuries.\par \par \uc2 Equity and bond funds saw outflows of $2.2 billion and $1.3 billion respectively in the week to June 10, according to banks citing EPFR data.\par \par \uc2 "The rest of the summer may continue to be challenging for emerging market fixed income assets," said \uc2 Barclays\uc2  in a client note.\par \par \uc2 "Growth concerns, overshadowed by the Fed's tapering of asset purchases and large EM fund outflows, are taking the front seat in our risk...metrics."\par \par \uc2 The Turkish lira edged towards recent record lows, despite more than $6 billion spent by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  in its support this week.\par \par \uc2 Concerns about the Fed's stimulus plans and anti-government protests across Turkey last month have driven the losses in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , leaving investors worried about the country's wide current account deficit and the lack of rate rises.\par \par \uc2 Benchmark bond yields fell almost 30 bps from the previous session however.\par \par \uc2 Most emerging European \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  were slightly weaker, though the forint briefly hit a three-week high.\par \par \uc2 (Reporting by Carolyn Cohn and Philip Baillie)\par \par \uc2 MARKETS-EMERGING | ABN | M | E | RBN | D | RNP | DNP | PTD   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020130715e97c000f0\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
