\par\par \b \uc2 Turkish Lira Extends Losses Despite  \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank Intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 By Prabha Natarajan and Erin McCarthy   \par \uc2 719 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 Juli 2013\par 21:13\par \uc2 Dow Jones Global Equities News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2013 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 The Turkish lira's losses couldn't be tamed Wednesday, despite continued \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by its \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Turkey\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  sold $1.3 billion at six separate \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  auctions Wednesday in an effort to halt the lira's precipitous slide against the dollar. For most of this week, \uc2 Turkey's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been actively trying to limit the lira's losses as it could trigger outflows and raise the cost of borrowing for the government.\par \par \uc2 Even measures to check speculative trading haven't been enough, however, to counter investors' growing wariness of Turkey and most emerging-market assets. Countries that have been particularly hit hard are those with current account deficits, like Turkey, India and Brazil.\par \par \uc2 "Everyone's... focusing on the fundamentals rather than on yields right now," said Win Thin, global head of emerging-market \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategy at \uc2 Brown Brothers Harriman\uc2  in New York.\par \par \uc2 The lira slid 0.6% against the dollar, which bought TRY1.9532, according to CQG.\par \par \uc2 On Wednesday, minutes of the Federal Reserve's June policy meeting showed about half of Fed officials believed the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  should end its $85 billion-a-month bond-buying program by the end of this year. The dollar pared some of its gains against some emerging-market \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  as the minutes also showed that some Fed officials didn't believe the labor market has improved enough for the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to start pulling back on its bond purchases.\par \par \uc2 But longer-term, the potential for Fed tapering has led investors to reduce their exposure to emerging markets, and as a result, asset prices are under pressure. In a vicious cycle, this leads to further widening of emerging economies' current account deficits and a weakening of their \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which makes refinancing existing debt more expensive for these countries.\par \par \uc2 "Barring any complete collapse of the U.S. economy in July or August, I think tapering's on track," Mr. Thin said. "Overall that's still dollar positive."\par \par \uc2 Brazil's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  also underperformed Wednesday, falling to its weakest level against the dollar since April 2009. That spurred the \uc2 Brazilian \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to call a snap auction of \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  swap contracts, which typically help support the real. Still, the real was 0.6% weaker against the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which bought BRL2.2735, according to CQG. \uc2 Brazil's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will conclude a rate-setting meeting later Wednesday, where it is widely expected by analysts to raise its benchmark Selic rate by at least 50 basis points to 8.5%.\par \par \uc2 The Mexican peso also weakened, slipping 0.5% against the dollar, which bought MXN12.9530.\par \par \uc2 Among Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the Indian rupee bounced back on Wednesday to trade below INR60 to the dollar for the first time since the release of strong U.S. payrolls data last week. The dollar recently traded at INR59.84, according to CQG data. The partial recovery came after the \uc2 Reserve Bank of India\uc2  took measures Tuesday to reduce volatility in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market and halt the rupee's relentless losses. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said Tuesday it had barred banks and \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealers from using their proprietary funds to trade in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  futures and options, though they can trade on behalf of their clients.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, China's weaker export data had little impact on other Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , as weaker growth in the Asian giant was mostly priced in.\par \par \uc2 Still, Indonesia, which has commodity trade ties to China, saw a weakening of its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The dollar was at IDR9965 against the rupiah, compared with IDR9959.0 the previous session, according to CQG data.\par \par \uc2 Indonesia also was in the market with an international bond issue. The sovereign bond had an initial guidance of 5.45% yield on the $500 million deal that could potentially increase, based on demand. The deal, rated BB+, is expected to price later Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 While investors may be willing to buy, the price they demand for the debt will be the highest Indonesia has paid since 2010, when it sold its 10-year bond at a 6% yield.\par \par \uc2 --Victoria McGrane contributed to this article.\par \par \uc2 Write to Prabha Natarajan at prabha.natarajan@dowjones.com and Erin McCarthy at erin.mccarthy@dowjones.com [ 10-07-13 1913GMT ]\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020130710e97a000og\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
