\par\par \b \uc2 *DJ \uc2 Turkey  \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank \highlight\uc2 : To Start Short-Term Monetary Tightening to Stabilize Lira\b0\par\par\uc2 291 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 11 Juni 2013\par 08:34\par \uc2 Dow Jones Newswires\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright (c) 2013, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 11 Jun 2013 02:36 EDT *DJ  \uc2 Turkey \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 : Will Tighten Through Open Market Transactions\par \par \uc2 11 Jun 2013 02:39 EDT *DJ  \b \highlight22\uc2 Turkey Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 : May Hold \b \highlight22\uc2 Forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  Sale Auctions, \b \highlight22\uc2 Intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  Directly If Needed\par \par \uc2 11 Jun 2013 03:10 EDT DJ  \uc2 Turkey \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 : to Start Short-Term Monetary Tightening to Stabilize Lira\par \par \uc2 ISTANBUL--\uc2 Turkey's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said Tuesday it will start additional short-term monetary tightening on days when deemed necessary to stabilize the lira and counter the impact of excessive \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market volatility on financial stability.\par \par \uc2 In a statement, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said it will tighten through open market transactions, reduce funding through the policy rate of 4.50% and it may hold \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  selling auctions and \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  directly on the market if needed.\par \par \uc2 The period of the tightening will depend on the volatility of the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, it said.\par \par \uc2 The Turkish lira rocketed higher in response to the signal from the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  that it has reached its limit for \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  weakness. At the outset of European trading, the lira sank to fresh 2011 lows, with the dollar trading almost at TRY1.91. But as the news from the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  emerged, the Turkish \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  then recovered sharply, with the dollar reading back down at TRY1.8964 by 0655 GMT. Meanwhile, the yield on two-year benchmark government bonds traded 17 basis points lower at 6.33%.\par \par \uc2 "It looks like we're in for another lively session" for the lira, \uc2 Citigroup\uc2  said in a note to clients.\par \par \uc2 Write to Yeliz Candemir at yeliz.candemir@dowjones.com\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 June 11, 2013 03:10 ET (07:10 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020130611e96b000qa\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
