\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE: \uc2 Turkey  \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank \highlight\uc2  Cuts Overnight Borrowing, Lending Rates\b0\par\par\uc2 By Yeliz Candemir and Emre Peker   \par \uc2 674 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 22 Januar 2013\par 16:57\par \uc2 Dow Jones News Service\par \uc2 DJ\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2013 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 ISTANBUL--\uc2 Turkey's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  continued to ease monetary policy on Tuesday as \uc2 Moody's Investors Service\uc2  suggested Ankara was edging closer to capturing an investment-grade credit rating, bolstering a growing investor confidence that the emerging economy is successfully managing its imbalances.\par \par \uc2 The bank stopped short of cutting its benchmark rate for a second consecutive month but surprised markets by reducing overnight borrowing and lending rates in a bid to prevent speculative capital inflows.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  cut its overnight borrowing rate to 4.75% from 5%, and its overnight lending rate to 8.75% from 9%, while holding its one-week benchmark interest rate steady at 5.5%, the bank said in a statement on its website.\par \par \uc2 The moves briefly sent stocks to a record high--extending a rally which has seen the IMKB index rise by 11% since the beginning of this year--and pulled the lira and bonds weaker. Turkish assets have been buoyed by anticipation of more investment-grade credit ratings following the November decision by \uc2 Fitch Ratings\uc2  that granted Turkey the first such status since 1994.\par \par \uc2 The 0.2% decline of the lira after the rate moves reversed earlier gains against the dollar spurred by an announcement from \uc2 Moody's\uc2  , which said ratings firm would hold a teleconference on Jan. 28 to discuss, among other things, Turkey "shifting closer to an investment grade sovereign rating".\par \par \uc2 Economists said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was likely trying to moderately weaken the lira to propel growth without spooking markets with a second consecutive cut to the benchmark rate.\par \par \uc2 "The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's signal via cutting the overnight borrowing rate hints that it will not allow Turkish lira to become an overvalued \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," said Ozgur Altug, chief economist with \uc2 BGC Partners\uc2  in Istanbul. "We think that the lira might be slightly under pressure, although the approaching \uc2 Moody's\uc2  conference will limit this pressure in the short-term."\par \par \uc2 The recent rally of the lira, which hit a ten month high against the dollar last week, prompted exporters to call for the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  and support the biggest factor in \b \highlight22\uc2 Turkey\b0 \highlight\uc2 's economic rebalancing: sales abroad. Companies argued that the lira's strength is beginning to undermine international competitiveness after record exports in 2012 helped Turkey narrow a record current-account deficit to 6.5% of gross domestic product from 10% of GDP in 2011.\par \par \uc2 Turkish Exporters Association Chairman \uc2 Mehmet Buyukeksi\uc2  said at the turn of the year that over appreciation of the lira would negatively affect the economy and exporters' competitive strength.\par \par \uc2 The call for a less valuable lira comes as the real effective exchange rate--the measure of the lira's strength against several other \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 --fell to 118.3 in December from a revised 119.4 in November.\par \par \uc2 In November, \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  Governor Erdem Basci said the monetary policy committee would gradually ease policy if the lira's real effective exchange rate continued to rose to a range of 120 to 125. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would take "strong" steps to halt the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's gains should the measure hit 130, he said, indicating the bank could consider interest rate cuts.\par \par \uc2 Some economists said by engaging in a limited easing, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was trying to keep its options open, but cautioned that the scope for further cuts was limited, given that a global recovery would spur credit growth, likely levy pressure on Turkey's key economic weakness: a bloated current account deficit.\par \par \uc2 "The bigger picture, however, is that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has only limited room to reduce market interest rates," said \uc2 Capital Economics\uc2 , the UK-based economic consultancy. "If anything, the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  Republic of Turkey would be more inclined to tighten policy to ensure that rising credit and domestic demand don't cause the current account deficit to widen to unsustainable levels."\par \par \uc2 Write to Yeliz Candemir at Yeliz.candemir@dowjones.com and Emre Peker at emre.peker@dowjones.com [ 01-22-13 1057ET ]\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJ00000020130122e91m000c3\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
