\par\par \b \uc2 *DJ IMF Paper Builds Case For Temporary Emerging-Market  \highlight22\uc2 FX Intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 507 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 29 Februar 2012\par 18:00\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2012, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 29 Feb 2012 12:00 EDT *DJ  IMF Paper: \b \highlight22\uc2 FX Intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  Can Help Build \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  Credibility\par \par \uc2 29 Feb 2012 12:00 EDT *DJ  IMF Paper: \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency Intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  Can Be Helpful Tool Against Volatility\par \par \uc2 29 Feb 2012 12:00 EDT *DJ  IMF Paper Counters Conventional View Of \b \highlight22\uc2 FX Intervention\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 29 Feb 2012 12:00 EDT *DJ  IMF \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  Study Includes Korea, Turkey, Poland, Brazil, Other Emerging Markets\par \par \uc2 29 Feb 2012 12:00 EDT *DJ  IMF Paper: Argues Against Sustained One-Way \b \highlight22\uc2 FX Intervention\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 29 Feb 2012 12:00 EDT *DJ  IMF Paper: \b \highlight22\uc2 FX Intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  Should Be To Realign \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Not Misalign\par \par \uc2 29 Feb 2012 12:19 EDT DJ  IMF Paper Builds Case For Temporary Emerging-Market \b \highlight22\uc2 FX Intervention\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 --IMF: \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  can be helpful tool against volatility\par \par \uc2 --IMF paper counters conventional view of \b \highlight22\uc2 FX intervention\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 --IMF study includes Korea, \b \highlight22\uc2 Turkey\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Poland, Brazil, other emerging markets\par \par \uc2 By Ian Talley\par \par \uc2 Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES\par \par \uc2 WASHINGTON (Dow Jones)--Turning decades of conventional wisdom on its head, a new research paper published Wednesday by International Monetary Fund economists builds a case for emerging markets to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in their exchange rates.\par \par \uc2 The IMF research paper advocates central banks in emerging markets smoothing out strong movements in their exchange rates, particularly when caused by external economic shocks that fuel hefty cash flows into or out of their economies.\par \par \uc2 The paper reflects a broader shift in IMF economic policy thinking that has given credence to some emerging market actions that have come under advanced-country censure, including a new backing of the use of capital controls.\par \par \uc2 "If two policy instruments are available (the policy interest rate and \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ), then they should be used in tandem to achieve both price-stability and exchange-rate objectives," the economists wrote.\par \par \uc2 In the paper, "Two Targets, Two Instruments: Monetary and Exchange Rate Policies in Emerging Market Economies," the economists argue that instead of undermining \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  credibility for inflation targeting--long a conventional view--\b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  can actually support \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  credibility. Such trust built by central banks makes their policies more effective.\par \par \uc2 "The idea of using more tools to address economic problems is one that has been gaining traction in the wake of the financial crisis," said Jonathan Ostry, deputy head of the research department and one of the three IMF economists who authored the paper.\par \par \uc2 "A narrow view in which all will be well as long as central banks deliver stable consumer prices simply doesn't hold water," he said.\par \par \uc2 The paper studied 14 countries and the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  policies, including Brazil, South Korea, Turkey, Poland, Hungary and Thailand. Many of the countries have come under criticism for their \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 In fact, the authors say that foreswearing \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the face of wild swings in \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  "might actually serve to undercut rather than boost credibility."\par \par \uc2 -By Ian Talley, Dow Jones Newswires, 202-862-9285; ian.talley@dowjones.com\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 February 29, 2012 12:19 ET (17:19 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020120229e82t005wj\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
