\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE:IMF Paper Advocates Temporary Emerging-Market  \highlight22\uc2 FX Intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 825 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 29 Februar 2012\par 19:39\par \uc2 Dow Jones Global Equities News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 --IMF: \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  can be helpful tool against volatility\par \par \uc2 --IMF paper counters conventional view of \b \highlight22\uc2 FX intervention\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 --IMF study includes Korea, \b \highlight22\uc2 Turkey\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Poland, Brazil, other emerging markets\par \par \uc2 (Adds IMF economists' comments, background and details throughout, starting in the third paragraph)\par \par \uc2 By Ian Talley\par \par \uc2 Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES\par \par \uc2 WASHINGTON (\uc2 Dow Jones\uc2 )--Turning decades of conventional wisdom on its head, a new research paper published Wednesday by \uc2 International Monetary Fund\uc2  economists builds a case for emerging markets to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in their \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The IMF research paper advocates central banks in emerging markets smoothing out strong movements in their exchange rates, particularly when caused by external economic shocks that fuel hefty cash flows into or out of their economies.\par \par \uc2 Far from being reluctant to use exchange rate \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , "central banks should embrace its use as being fully consistent" with inflation-targeting, the economists said.\par \par \uc2 The paper reflects a broader shift in IMF economic policy thinking, giving credence to some emerging-market actions that have come under advanced-country censure, including a new backing of the use of capital controls.\par \par \uc2 "If two policy instruments are available (the policy interest rate and \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ), then they should be used in tandem to achieve both price-stability and exchange-rate objectives," the economists wrote.\par \par \uc2 In the paper, "Two Targets, Two Instruments: Monetary and Exchange Rate Policies in Emerging Market Economies," the economists argue that instead of undermining \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  credibility for inflation targeting--long a conventional view--\b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  can actually support \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  credibility. Such trust built by central banks makes their policies more effective.\par \par \uc2 "The idea of using more tools to address economic problems is one that has been gaining traction in the wake of the financial crisis," said Jonathan Ostry, deputy head of the research department and one of the three IMF economists who wrote the paper.\par \par \uc2 "A narrow view in which all will be well as long as central banks deliver stable consumer prices simply doesn't hold water," he said.\par \par \uc2 The paper studied 14 countries and their \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  policies, including Brazil, South Korea, Turkey, Poland, Hungary and Thailand. Many of the countries have come under criticism for their \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 In fact, the authors say that forswearing \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the face of wild swings in \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  "might actually serve to undercut rather than boost credibility."\par \par \uc2 The authors argued against sustained exchange rate \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , saying it would prove too costly to an economy. Rather, under permanent market pressures, policy makers should allow the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to adjust. Unlike Brazil or South Korea, which are largely recognized as floating economies despite some \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , China's yuan has long been seen as persistently undervalued as the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  buys foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and sells yuan to give it a competitive advantage.\par \par \uc2 "You should not be \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  to sustain a misaligned exchange rate, you should be \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  to mitigate misalignment," Ostry said.\par \par \uc2 Emerging markets are particularly exposed to large international capital flows because government balance sheets don't have the depth to offset such investments and their economies aren't as flexible as industrialized countries. Like reeds in the wind, emerging markets have had to weather massive capital movements in the wake of the 2008 financial crisis and euro debt woes.\par \par \uc2 The Institute of International Finance, an industry group representing more than 400 of the world's largest financial firms, expects capital flows to emerging markets to fall this year by an estimated $164 billion, contributing to a near-30% plummet in cash flows to those regions since 2010. That's likely to mean continuing pressure on their exchange rates. Earlier this month, Brazil's finance minister revived fears of an international \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  war.\par \par \uc2 But the IMF staff said that as long as countries are simply seeking to return their \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  back into equilibrium with underlying economic fundamentals, \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  can play a stabilizing role in regional and global economies. By combining \b \highlight22\uc2 forex intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  with policy-rate decisions, central banks can afford to weaken their rate actions to achieve the same objective. That prevents a competition of too-low interest rates across emerging markets and avoid the resulting competitive \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the authors say.\par \par \uc2 The shift in perspective also highlights the growing say of emerging markets within the fund and the academic fallout from the financial crisis that eroded many long-held economist assumptions. The condoning of \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 --on a limited basis--addresses complaints from many developing countries that advanced nations should take into account the international impacts of monetary and economic policy. Brazil, for example, repeatedly cited the U.S. Federal Reserve's easing as helping to drive capital flows damaging to its economy. Brazil has \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to prevent the real from further harm, drawing criticism from abroad.\par \par \uc2 -By Ian Talley, Dow Jones Newswires, 202-862-9285; ian.talley@dowjones.com\par \par \uc2 On the Web: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.imf.org/external/pubs/ft/sdn/2012/sdn1201.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://www.imf.org/external/pubs/ft/sdn/2012/sdn1201.pdf }}}\uc2  [ 29-02-12 1839GMT ]\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020120229e82t001ed\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw427\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal6405\pichgoal600
