\par\par \b \uc2 *DJ Turkey  \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank \highlight\uc2  Governor Content With Lira Rise\b0\par\par\uc2 931 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 30 Januar 2012\par 09:01\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2012, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 30 Jan 2012 03:01 EDT *DJ  Turkey Bank Governor Cautions On Inflation\par \par \uc2 30 Jan 2012 03:01 EDT *DJ  Turkey Bank Governor: Could Rebuild \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  Reserves If Confidence Persists\par \par \uc2 30 Jan 2012 03:01 EDT *DJ  Turkey Bank Governor: Need Time For Inflation To Fall\par \par \uc2 30 Jan 2012 03:01 EDT *DJ  Turkey Bank Governor: Price Stability To Be Main Focus Of 2012\par \par \uc2 30 Jan 2012 03:01 EDT *DJ  Turkey Bank Governor: 'More Optimistic' On Euro Zone, Global Growth\par \par \uc2 30 Jan 2012 03:01 EDT *DJ  Turkey Bank Governor: Growth Will Follow Europe's Austerity Drive\par \par \uc2 30 Jan 2012 03:01 EDT DJ  Turkey \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  Governor Content With Lira's Rise\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par    By Geoffrey T. Smith and Joe Parkinson \par    Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 DAVOS, Switzerland (Dow Jones)--Turkey's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  governor said this weekend that he is happy with the lira's recent surge as it should push down on inflation, but cautioned that prices could remain elevated this year, possibly preventing the bank from loosening policy if sentiment turns negative.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Speaking in an interview with Dow Jones Newswires at the World Economic Forum meeting in Davos, Switzerland, Governor Erdem Basci offered a robust defense of Turkey's controversial monetary policy, stressing that the bank's moves had last year simultaneously pushed the lira lower to help exports, popped a burgeoning consumer lending bubble that threatened to destabilize the economy and improved Turkey's mushrooming current account deficit. That deficit is currently almost 10% of gross domestic product and is considered a key weakness of the economy by investors.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The governor stressed the lira's recent rise, gaining some 5% against the dollar since the beginning of the year, meant that the bank had stopped selling its scarce foreign \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  reserves and could begin rebuilding them if global confidence remained optimistic.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "We are content with the appreciation, to speed up disinflation. Just by base effects, inflation is going to fall by 3 percentage points, but for the rest we need time. The earlier the fall in inflation starts, the better," Basci said.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "Price stability will be the main focus of attention this year," the governor added.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Basci's comments come amid a surge in the value of Turkey's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  since the beginning of 2012. Last year, the lira weakened more than any \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the world versus the dollar. Since January it has posted one of the world's strongest performances, buoyed by rising global sentiment and last week's \f28 \uc2 \f2 Federal Reserve\f28 \uc2 \f2  move to boost liquidity.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The rising lira should help push down inflation, which hit 10.45% on the year in December, moving into double digits for the first time in three years and feeding fears of a pronounced rise in prices. But pressures keeping prices elevated later this year could hinder the bank from responding to potential shocks from the euro zone or other events that may decrease global risk appetite.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Tighter policy could keep upward pressure on the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , cutting into the competitiveness of Turkish exporters and making imports more costly; adding upward pressure to the economy's gaping current account deficit.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Despite that prospect, Basci said that he had become "rather more optimistic" about the prospects for solving the crisis in the euro zone after several top policy makers from some of the bloc's new governments assured him of their commitment to fiscal consolidation.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "Now it seems that there is a unanimous voice and determination about fiscal austerity. All the new governments have the same opinion that fiscal contraction would help rather than hurt," the bank chief said, adding that "now everybody talks like a German."\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Emerging markets across the world may be enjoying a robust rally, but not all investors share Basci's confidence that Turkey's stellar start to the year is sustainable. Some caution that the recent rebound of the lira and Turkish bonds hasn't been driven by a shift in investor perceptions of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Turkey\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , but by hefty \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central-bank intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and a recovery in risk appetite.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The cost of insuring Turkish debt has firmed, underlining investor skepticism that Turkey's imbalances are no longer a risk. Governor Basci's strong \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the markets in January was deemed necessary despite the bank tightening its policy through an unconventional widening of its interest-rate corridor, which allows it to constantly shift the cost of borrowing between 5.75% and 12.5%, rather than raising benchmark interest rates, which remain at a record low of 5.75%.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  may have shored up the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , but concerns over fundamentals, policy priorities and external risks mean that if sentiment turns negative, Turkish assets could be back in the crosshairs.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Meanwhile, the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's increasingly complex economic policy has fed investor fears that the economy, which grew at an 8.2% pace in the third quarter, could be headed for a hard landing. Although the governor is more upbeat than many international investors, he concedes that Turkish debt is unlikely to be elevated to investment grade any time soon.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Top Turkish policy makers have long berated ratings firms for what they see as a perceived bias against Turkey, which has posted remarkable economic growth as it rebounded from a steep recession in 2009.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "It's a little bit too early to talk about" an investment-grade rating," the governor said.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -By Joe Parkinson and Geoffrey T. Smith, Dow Jones Newswires, +905306130065, geoffrey.smith@dowjones.com\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 January 30, 2012 03:01 ET (08:01 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020120130e81u0028h\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
