\par\par \b \uc2 *DJ Turkey  \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank \highlight\uc2  To Hold $50M Intraday  \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2  Auction\b0\par\par\uc2 259 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 9 Januar 2012\par 09:18\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2012, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 9 Jan 2012 03:37 EDT *DJ  Turkey \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  Sells $50M At Intraday \b \highlight22\uc2 Forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  Auction\par \par \uc2 9 Jan 2012 03:48 EDT *DJ  Turkey \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  To Hold $50M Intraday \b \highlight22\uc2 Forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  Auction\par \par \uc2 9 Jan 2012 04:11 EDT *DJ  Turkey \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  Sells $50M At Intraday \b \highlight22\uc2 Forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  Auction\par \par \uc2 9 Jan 2012 04:34 EDT DJ  Turkey \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  Sells $100M At Two Intraday \b \highlight22\uc2 Forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  Auctions\par \par \uc2 ISTANBUL (Dow Jones)--Turkey's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  Monday sold $100 million at two unscheduled intraday \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  auctions to support the lira.\par \par \uc2 The bank received total bids of $324 million at the auctions.\par \par \uc2 On Friday, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said it would hold intraday unscheduled \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  auctions "when necessary," in the latest move to shore up the embattled lira. The bank said each auction amount would be $50 million from Jan. 6, and would take place "in order to support additional monetary tightening."\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Turkey\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  significantly in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets in recent days to control a slide in the lira. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said Friday it had sold around $15 billion since August and \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  Governor Erdem Basci said Friday policy makers would allow the Turkish lira to appreciate this year, reversing its sharp drop in 2011.\par \par \uc2 At 0925 GMT, Turkish lira was trading at 1.8718 against the dollar.\par \par \uc2 -By Yeliz Candemir, Dow Jones Newswires, +90 535 432 05 91; yeliz.candemir@dowjones.com\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 January 09, 2012 04:34 ET (09:34 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020120109e819001fr\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
