\par\par \b \uc2 DJ Turkey's  \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank \highlight\uc2  Keeps Up Fight To Prevent Lira Weakness\b0\par\par\uc2 604 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 4 Januar 2012\par 18:01\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2012, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 -- Turkey's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  continued its fight to prevent further lira appreciation Wednesday\par \par \uc2 -- The bank \b \highlight22\uc2 intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  for the fourth trading session and conducts a daily \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  selling auction\par \par \uc2 -- Concerns rising the banks reserves are being depleted too quickly \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par    By Yeliz Candemir and Clare Connaghan \par    Of \f28 \uc2 \f2 DOW JONES NEWSWIRES\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 LONDON (\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 )--Turkey's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  kept up its fight to prevent a precipitous slide in its \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Wednesday but with foreign-\f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  reserves being quickly depleted doubts are surfacing over how long they can keep up this aggressive assault.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 For the fourth straight session, the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  of the Republic of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Turkey\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  propped up the lira by directly \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervening\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign-exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market and selling $100 million at its daily \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign-exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  selling auction.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "While Turkey's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  measures might support the lira short-term, it is however questionable how long the bank will be able to continue with these levels of foreign-\f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  sales without depleting its foreign-\f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  reserves too quickly," said Carolin Hecht, a \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  strategist at \f28 \uc2 \f2 Commerzbank\f28 \uc2 \f2  in Frankfurt.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Prior to Wednesday, the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  is estimated to have spent around $4.5 billion in just three trading days via direct \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  selling auctions to limit depreciation of the Turkish lira.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "There is a considerable meltdown in \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  reserves.... Foreign capital inflows are limited and the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  needs its \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  reserves," said Mehmet Besimoglu, chief economist with Oyak Research.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 According to the latest data, the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  reserves were $82.8 billion in the week to Dec. 23.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The lira sunk to a fresh record low against the dollar last week as investor concerns mounted over the prospect of the fast-growing economy overheating and effects of the intensifying euro crisis. With fears over the impact this could have on inflation, which broke double digits in December, the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  stepped in Friday and launched a large-scale \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  for only the second time in five years.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The bank has directly \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in every trading session since Friday, keeping up its strong opposition to lira weakness. In further measures to prop up the lira, the bank has continued to hold its daily \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign-exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  auctions.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "We assume that it will use its ammunition more carefully over the coming days, which is likely to disappoint some market participants," said Hecht.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Signs of this are already emerging given that Wednesday's dollar-selling auction was much lower than Friday's $750 million. In addition, the bank's direct \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  also appears to be on a much smaller scale Wednesday, traders said.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Should this continue, the lira is likely to come under further pressure, according to market participants. In fact this already looks to be the case with the Turkish \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  trading down around 1% against the buck Wednesday.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Turkey's central has been under fire for months by some economists, who say the bank has been too sanguine about inflation risks and too reluctant to increase its central policy rate.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Instead, the bank has pursued a less orthodox policy, tightening monetary policy by varying overnight borrowing rates for commercial banks within a wide corridor of 5.75% to 12.5%, while leaving the main policy rate unchanged.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 At 1658 GMT, the dollar was trading at TRY1.8834 against the Turkish lira compared with TRY1.8738 late Tuesday in New York.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -By Yeliz Candemir and Clare Connaghan, Dow Jones Newswires; +44 (0) 20 7842 9496, clare.connaghan@dowjones.com\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\f28 \par