\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 2- \highlight22\uc2 Turkey \highlight\uc2 's lira firms on c.bank  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2 , shares jump\b0\par\par\uc2 643 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 3 Januar 2012\par 11:45\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  sells $350 million at auction\par \par \uc2 * Sells estimated $400 million more through direct \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 * Shares nearly 3 pct up on global recovery\par \par \uc2 * Yields up on tight liquidity, high funding costs\par \par \uc2 * December CPI rose 0.58 pct mth/mth, 10.45 pct yr/yr\par \par \uc2 (Adds further \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , closing prices, quotes)\par \par \uc2 ISTANBUL, Jan 3 (Reuters) - Repeated \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  helped the Turkish lira firm below 1.88 against the dollar on Tuesday, while shares benefitted from a recovery in global risk appetite to gain nearly 3 percent.\par \par \uc2 The Turkish lira traded at 1.8765 in late trade compared with 1.8900 on Monday afternoon, but it was unable to hold onto its strongest level of 1.8697.\par \par \uc2 Since last Friday, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has sold between $4-4.5 billion through direct \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market and in daily \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  auctions to support the ailing lira.\par \par \uc2 On Tuesday, the bank sold $350 million at auction and traders reckoned it sold a further $400 million in several bouts of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The bank confirmed \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market, without disclosing amounts sold.\par \par \uc2 The lira weakened nearly 22 percent versus the dollar in 2011, adding to inflationary pressures, and on Dec. 28 hit its weakest ever level of 1.9215 against the greenback.\par \par \uc2 Against its euro-dollar basket, the lira was quoted at 2.1595 in late trade, compared with 2.1676 late Monday. At its strongest, the lira strengthened to as much as 2.1481 against the basket, coming down from 2.1731 earlier.\par \par \uc2 "For the moment, neither the \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  sales nor the tightening in lira liquidity had significant impact on the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The lira basket \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  (0.5 dollar-lira + 0.5 euro-lira) declined by 0.5 percent in a day to 2.16 vicinity, but this was also related with the strengthening risk appetite in international markets," said Erkin Isik, a strategist at TEB-\uc2 BNP Paribas\uc2 .\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  Governor Erdem Basci said last week the bank may sell foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  directly on "exceptional days", without specifying what would make a day exceptional.\par \par \uc2 During a meeting with economists on Tuesday, the bank said unsterilized \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  sales and \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  could be used to complement monetary tightening.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  can decide not to sterilize \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  sales by not providing the amount of lira drained from the market through repo auctions, decreasing lira liquidity in the market.\par \par \uc2 Istanbul's main stock index closed 2.96 percent up at 52,859.07 points, outperforming the MSCI emerging markets index, which was up 2.52 percent.\par \par \uc2 "The increase is mostly related with recovery of the global risk sentiment. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  and the increase of daily \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  selling auctions amounts also supported the index," said Serdar Pazi, fund manager at Ata Invest.\par \par \uc2 Shares of Turkish lender \uc2 Yapi Kredi\uc2  rose 7.04 percent on Tuesday and banking index surged 4.04 percent as the lira's strengthening supported banking shares, analysts said. Foreign investment in Turkish shares is concentrated in the banking sector.\par \par \uc2 The yield on Turkey's benchmark bond maturing on Dec. 4, 2013 closed at 11.53 percent, up from a previous close of 11.48 percent.\par \par \uc2 "The increase of funding costs resulted in a sell-off in front-end of the yield curve. So long as the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  increases the funding yield above 5.75 percent, it's hard to see bond yields declining," said a fixed income trader of a bank.\par \par \uc2 Turkey's consumer price index rose 0.58 percent month-on-month in December, exceeding a Reuters poll forecast of a 0.3 percent rise, for a year-on-year rise of 10.45 percent, data showed on Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 (Writing by Seltem Iyigun; Editing by Simon Cameron-Moore)\par \par \uc2 MARKETS-TURKEY/ (UPDATE 2)   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020120106e813000j4\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
