\par\par \b \uc2 Emerging-Market  \highlight22\uc2 Currencies \highlight\uc2 , Debt Rally On Positive Global Data\b0\par\par\uc2 1,579 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 3 Januar 2012\par 21:44\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 --Latin American \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  lead emerging-market \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  rally\par \par \uc2 --Emerging-market debt strengthens\par \par \uc2 --Hungarian assets underperform on uncertainty about government policies\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par    By Erin McCarthy \par    Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 NEW YORK (Dow Jones)--Emerging-market \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and debt kicked off 2012 stronger, as positive global economic data boosted market optimism.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Some Latin American \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  jumped about 2% against the dollar, while emerging European \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  also bounced back from last week's weaker levels. The Hungarian forint, however, was an outlier, again punished for concerns surrounding recent government policy making.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Emerging-market sovereign debt strengthened across the board, with the premium investors demand to hold such debt shrinking modestly. The spread on the \f28 \uc2 \f2 J.P. Morgan\f28 \uc2 \f2  Emerging Markets Bond Index Global, or Embig, tightened by eight basis points to 418 basis points over Treasurys. In price terms, its index rose 0.1%.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Venezuela and Argentina's debt outperformed, as they often outpace wider market swings. Argentina's spread shed 24 basis points to 902 basis points over Treasurys, and its index jumped 1.8%. Venezuela's spread narrowed by 25 basis points to 1234 basis points over Treasurys, while its index climbed 0.9%.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Helping prop up riskier assets was a slew of better-than-expected economic data. An official reading of China's purchasing managers' index released over the weekend showed manufacturing activity swung from a contraction to a mild expansion in December, while data showed unemployment in Germany falling more than expected last month. In the U.S., the manufacturing sector expanded in December, according to data released Tuesday, which added to the improved market sentiment.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Analysts warn, however, that the positive start to the year for emerging market \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  may only be temporary.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "It's a bit of a risk-on move but it's definitely not going to last," said Carolin Hecht, emerging markets strategist at \f28 \uc2 \f2 Commerzbank\f28 \uc2 \f2 , who warns that euro-zone debt crisis concerns will likely return to the forefront.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Still, investors took advantage of the risk rally. The Brazilian real and Mexican peso both soared about 2% against the U.S. \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , tracking gains in U.S. stocks. The real hit a three-week high against the dollar, which traded 2.1% lower at BRL1.8320 late Tuesday, according to CQG. Against the peso, the dollar slid 2% to MXN13.6494 from MXN13.9224 late Monday.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Turkish lira also bounced against the dollar, but largely in response to \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Turkey\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  waded into the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market Tuesday for a third straight day to support the lira, and also sold $350 million at its daily \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  auction. Turkey's relentless inflation rate, which hit a three-year high in December, and large current account deficit have pushed investors to punish the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in recent months. The dollar slid 1.2% against the lira to TRY1.8716, according to CQG.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Hungarian forint, however, could not latch on to the general risk rally, as investors continue to flee the country's assets on concerns about its government's unpredictable economic policies. The forint fell to a five-week low against the euro Tuesday, while the cost of insuring Hungarian debt against default hit a record high. On the Embig, Hungary's spread widened by a whopping 46 basis points to 651 basis points over Treasurys, while its index dove 3% in price.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The government's defiant passage, despite criticism from the European Union and the International Monetary Fund, of a \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  bill that analysts say undermines the independence of Hungary's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , has made foreign investors wary. Earlier in December, the EU and IMF broke off informal talks on a possible aid package for debt-laden Hungary due to the proposed bill. Uncertainty whether the talks will resume has put Hungarian assets under further pressure.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Hungary's government is "continuing their very explosive fiscal policy measures," said \f28 \uc2 \f2 Commerzbank\f28 \uc2 \f2 's Hecht. "Certainly it will be very difficult for the Hungarian government to get IMF aid now."\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -By Erin McCarthy, \f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones Newswires\f28 \uc2 \f2 ; 212-416-2712; erin.mccarthy@dowjones.com; @djfxtrader [ 03-01-12 2044GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 --Hungary's policy missteps lead to massive selloff\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 --Investors forcing government to accept external help\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 --Key trigger is if there is no deal with IMF\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par    By Erin McCarthy and Prabha Natarajan \par    Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 NEW YORK (Dow Jones)--Hungary stands at the brink of a \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  crisis, leaving its government little time or room to reverse policy missteps that have prompted a massive selloff in the forint.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Market participants are consciously pushing the government against a wall by ridding themselves of the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , which hit an all-time low of HUF321.67 against the euro Wednesday. With the forint falling nearly 1% or more daily, local government bonds yields trading in the double digits, and the government meeting with the International Monetary Fund in a matter of days, Hungary's make-or-break moment may soon be approaching.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "We are on the road to a \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  crisis, but we haven't arrived there yet," said Viktor Szabo, portfolio manager at \f28 \uc2 \f2 Aberdeen Asset Management\f28 \uc2 \f2 . "The markets are forcing the government to accept external help."\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The risks intensified talks over a precautionary credit line from the European Union and IMF broken down because of the government's move to strip the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  of some of its independence. While markets still expect Hungary to wrangle a credit line of at least 15 to 20 billion euros, a definitive failure to achieve that could send the forint into a freefall.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "The key trigger is basically when it becomes fully evident there can't be compromise," said Peter Attard Montalto, emerging markets economist at Nomura.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Aberdeen Asset Management\f28 \uc2 \f2 's Szabo believes the evaporating confidence could feed on itself in \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  markets.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "If [the forint] starts to lose 1-2% of its \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  value daily, that's what I would call a crisis," he said. "A couple of more days like this week is bad for Hungary and the forint."\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 That critical juncture could come on Jan. 11, when a delegation from Budapest is expected to visit IMF chief \f28 \uc2 \f2 Christine Lagarde\f28 \uc2 \f2  in Washington. The IMF has said next week's meetings aren't negotiations, and no decision has been made on resuming formal talks.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 If nothing pans out from these meetings, it could set off a selloff that could widen risk premiums by as much as 200 basis points on local government bonds and depreciate the forint to HUF340 against the euro, wrote Michal Dybula, an economist at \f28 \uc2 \f2 BNP Paribas\f28 \uc2 \f2  in Warsaw, in a note to clients. This would push Hungary into a deeper recession with a negative economic growth of 3% for this year, he said.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Another focal point for those betting against the forint: Hungary's shaky balance sheet. Its \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  holds only EUR2.5 billion in cash reserves and yet this year some EUR4.3 billion in foreign debt will mature (most of it owed to the EU and IMF) with a further EUR5.5 billion of local debt also falling due.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Add to this the risk of more sovereign ratings downgrades for Hungary to compound those announced by \f28 \uc2 \f2 Standard & Poor's\f28 \uc2 \f2  and Moodys Investors Service late last year and the pressure is on for large holders of Hungarian debt--among them the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Templeton Global Bond Fund\f28 \uc2 \f2 , which held $3.35 billion as of Sept. 30, 2011.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Analysts say the government could potentially fund itself with short-term debt issuance until at least the third quarter, but after a series of failed debt auctions, yields are now above 10% for 10-year debt, a level that's fundamentally unsustainable.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Alternatively, Hungary could raise interest rates to attract capital back into the country and boost the forint--and it is expected to do so the tune of 50 basis points on Jan. 24. But that will only worsen an already deteriorating economic outlook.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Against such risks, both sides in the EU-IMF standoff with Hungary have strong incentives to compromise.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 A sharp drop in the forint would hurt Austrian and Italian banks with a strong presence in Hungarian assets, adding to contagion risks in a euro zone that is grappling with its own nail-biting crisis. But it would also be a political blow for the government as it would stoke inflation for Hungarian households and could add to the domestic unrest that is already burgeoning in the country.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Partly because neither side is expected to be suicidal and partly because Hungary, despite everything, is seen with the potential for rapid growth over the long term, some long-only investment funds have held onto their positions in Hungarian debt.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 It's "not that we are impressed by government initiatives so far," but rather that "we see longer-term value at these valuations," said Michael Hansen, strategic portfolio manager at Global Evolution A/S, a Denmark hedge fund with $40 million in Hungarian assets.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Nonetheless, both \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and bond markets are signaling anxiety over how much capital flight will be needed before Hungary backtracks on its policy stance to achieve rapprochement with the IMF and EU.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "You actually have to have the crisis" before you get the support from the IMF, said Nomura's Montalto.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -By Erin McCarthy and Prabha Natarajan, \f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones Newswires\f28 \uc2 \f2 ; 212-416-2712; erin.mccarthy@dowjones.com\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 --Gordon Fairclough, Veronika Gulyas and Jessica Mead contributed to this article. [ 04-01-12 2244GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020120103e813000sw\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
