\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 2-Turkey gives lira brief boost; stocks end year down\b0\par\par\uc2 519 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 30 Dezember 2011\par 10:36\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * Lira dips to 1.85 after \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  before easing\par \par \uc2 * Volume of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  estimated at least $3 bln\par \par \uc2 * C.bank sells high volume of dollars at \b \highlight22\uc2 fx\b0 \highlight\uc2  auction\par \par \uc2 * Yields steady, volume thin\par \par \uc2 * Shares dip\par \par \uc2 (Adds closing prices, fresh quotes)\par \par \uc2 ISTANBUL, Dec 30 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  boosted the Turkish lira as far as 1.8510 against the dollar on Friday but the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  later surrendered much of its gains, while the main stock index ended 2011 trading with losses of about 22 percent.\par \par \uc2 By 1555 GMT, the lira traded at 1.8882 per dollar, well off a record low of 1.9215 hit in late trade on Wednesday due to concerns about monetary policy measures but also some 22 percent weaker compared with end-2010.\par \par \uc2 It firmed as far as 2.1296 against its euro-dollar basket\par \par \uc2 right after Friday's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , from 2.1977 earlier and a previous close of 2.1992.\par \par \uc2 "As the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  started after the lira weakened above the 2.20 level versus the (euro-dollar) basket, we can talk about this level as the red line of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," said Tufan Comert, a strategist at Garanti Securities.\par \par \uc2 "Markets anticipate the size of the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  as $2.5-3 billion but the lira eased again to 1.88-1.89 band versus the dollar. This shows \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  wasn't effective," he added.\par \par \uc2 Traders told Reuters the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  sold at least $3 billion during the direct \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Friday. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  last \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  directly in the \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  market on Oct. 18, selling $525 million.\par \par \uc2 Istanbul's main stock index ended the year's last trading day down 22.3 percent from the end of 2010 and down 1.51 percent on the day at 51,266.62 points.\par \par \uc2 It looked set to slightly underperform the MSCI emerging markets index, which was heading for losses of just over 20 percent on the year.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 FX INTERVENTION\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  sold $750 million in its \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  auction on Friday. Around the time the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  began, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  issued a statement saying it will continue to hold \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2 -selling auctions on days when it \b \highlight22\uc2 intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  directly in the \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  market.\par \par \uc2 The yield on \b \highlight22\uc2 Turkey\b0 \highlight\uc2 's benchmark bond maturing on Dec. 4, 2013 closed at 11.48 percent in extremely thin trading, compared with a previous close at 10.98 percent.\par \par \uc2 The Turkish \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  also held a one-month repo auction maturing on Jan. 27 with a volume of 3 billion lira ($1.56 billion) and an average rate of 11.34 percent, bank data showed , and injected 2 billion lira into the market in a one-week intraday repo auction at a simple rate of 11.55 percent.\par \par \uc2 Turkish markets shrugged off data showing Turkey's trade deficit narrowed 2.8 percent year-on-year in November to $7.533 billion, data showed, less than a forecast deficit of $8.15 billion in a Reuters poll.\par \par \uc2 (Writing by Seltem Iyigun; Editing by Daren Butler/Ruth Pitchford)\par \par \uc2 MARKETS-TURKEY/ (UPDATE 2)   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020120102e7cu0009u\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
