\par\par \b \uc2 Emerging Europe  \highlight22\uc2 Currencies \highlight\uc2  Fall; Emerging-Market Debt Down\b0\par\par\uc2 By Erin McCarthy   \par \uc2 Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES   \par \uc2 620 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 30 Dezember 2011\par 20:48\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 NEW YORK (Dow Jones)--Emerging European central banks took advantage of light trading conditions to prop up their \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  Friday, after the region's \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  came under pressure.\par \par \uc2 Both \b \highlight22\uc2 Turkey\b0 \highlight\uc2  and Poland were seen \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, as their \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  underperformed despite quiet trading. No one, however, came to the rescue of the Hungarian forint, which fell more than 1.5% against the euro on Friday.\par \par \uc2 Latin American \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  made only modest gains on the last trading day of 2011, while emerging-market sovereign debt weakened slightly.\par \par \uc2 Analysts say that markets could demonstrate more negative sentiment when trading picks up next week, and emerging-market \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , especially in Europe, could see more downward pressure. Meanwhile, the euro-zone sovereign debt crisis remains in focus, as France and Germany both have government debt auctions next week. Emerging-market \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 ' performances have largely been taking cues from external developments for much of this year.\par \par \uc2 "The market risk is still the main factor," said Ilan Solot, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at \uc2 Brown Brothers Harriman\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, the premium that investors demand to hold emerging-market debt increased slightly Friday. The spread on the \uc2 J.P. Morgan\uc2  Emerging Markets Bond Index Global, or Embig, widened by six basis points to 425 basis points over Treasurys. In price terms, its index was flat. Egypt's debt was little changed despite a cut further into junk territory for its credit ratings from Fitch Ratings on Friday.\par \par \uc2 Among \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the Turkish lira soared after Turkey's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  held a $750 million dollar-selling auction and \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  directly in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market. Investors have favored shorting the lira this year because of Turkey's large current account deficit, the central's bank unique monetary policy mix and concerns about inflation.\par \par \uc2 The dollar slid 1.3% against the lira to TRY1.8927, according to CQG.\par \par \uc2 Poland also took steps to rescue its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  from further weakness for a second day in a row, in order to keep its foreign debt at bay and avoid the necessity of introducing painful austerity measures.\par \par \uc2 The foreign debt, making up for around one-third of Poland's total public debt, is priced based on the zloty's last fixing each year. To strengthen the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  just ahead of that time, the finance ministry's agent, BGK bank, was heavily buying zlotys. The zloty was still down more than 1% against the euro, which traded at PLN4.4685 from PLN4.4072 late Thursday.\par \par \uc2 The Hungarian forint slid to a five-week low against the euro, after Hungary's parliament passed a controversial \b \highlight22\uc2 central-bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  law Friday that the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the European Commission and the International Monetary Fund have criticized for threatening the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's independence. The defiance of Hungary's government in pushing the bill forward could derail the country's bid for financial support from the IMF and European Union, analysts say.\par \par \uc2 "The IMF deal went from being uncertain to very unlikely to happen, at least in the short term," Solot said. On the Embig, Hungary's debt weakened significantly, its spread widening by 22 basis points to 624 basis points over Treasurys. Its index dove 1.2% in price.\par \par \uc2 In Latin America, the Mexican peso advanced mildly against the dollar in thin trading, while Brazil's real was nearly flat against the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the day. Both \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  posted a depreciation of more than 12% against the dollar this year, according to CQG.\par \par \uc2 -By Erin McCarthy, Dow Jones Newswires; 212-416-2712; erin.mccarthy@dowjones.com\par \par \uc2 --Yeliz Candemir and Patryk Wasilewski contributed to this article. [ 30-12-11 1948GMT ]\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020111230e7cu000kp\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
