\par\par \b \uc2 2nd UPDATE:  \highlight22\uc2 Turkey Central Bank \highlight\uc2  Keeps  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2  To Boost Lira\b0\par\par\uc2 442 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 30 Dezember 2011\par 18:00\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 (Rewrites throughout, adding details including \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's further \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  and updating \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  level.)\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par     By Yeliz Candemir \par     Of \f28 \uc2 \f2 DOW JONES NEWSWIRES\f28 \par \par \uc2 ISTANBUL (Dow Jones)--The \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  of the Republic of \b \highlight22\uc2 Turkey\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Friday kept \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  intermittently in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to support Turkish lira, the bank confirmed, strengthening the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to as much as 1.8510 against the dollar.\par \par \uc2 Recently, the Turkish lira was trading at TRY1.8907 against the dollar, after a series of \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  later confirmed in an emailed statement that it had \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market due to "unhealthy price moves." However, the statement didn't make explicit the size of Friday's direct \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , and a bank spokesman declined to give the size.\par \par \uc2 Traders reported that the bank began selling dollars Friday afternoon local time, strengthening the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  by more than 3% to below TRY1.86 to the dollar. In addition to direct \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the bank sold $750 million at its daily \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  auction to stem the lira's sharp decline. In an earlier statement, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said it will continue to hold \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  auctions when it directly \b \highlight22\uc2 intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market. The size of Friday's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , including the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's daily \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  auction, was around $2.5 billion to $3 billion, traders said.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  "is very aggressive in the \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  market in the last trading day of the year," said Ozgur Altug, chief economist at \uc2 BGC Partners\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Analysts said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  seems to be determined to support lira with aggressive \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 "The reason behind the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's aggressive \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  selling today may be heavy foreign demand and its aim to pull down USD/TRY," said Tufan Comert, an analyst with Garanti Yatirim.\par \par \uc2 Turkish stocks also tumbled and the main IMKB 100 index closed 1.5% lower at 51266.6 in the last trading day of the year after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The last time the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  directly \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market was Oct. 18.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Turkey\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor, Erdem Basci, on Wednesday said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  directly in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market on an exceptional basis, without clarifying how the bank would classify trading days as normal or exceptional. However, the lira's downward move intensified recently after the comments from Turkey's head central banker generated some confusion.\par \par \uc2 Turkish lira has lost nearly 20% of its value against the dollar since the beginning of 2011.\par \par \uc2 -By Yeliz Candemir, Dow Jones Newswires; +90 535 432 05 91; yeliz.candemir@dowjones.com [ 30-12-11 1700GMT ]\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020111230e7cu000j8\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
