\par\par \b \uc2 WORLD  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 : Euro Suffers Year-End Blues; Turkish Lira Soars\b0\par\par\uc2 541 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 30 Dezember 2011\par 12:48\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 --Euro falls to lowest level against yen since June 2001, below Y100\par \par \uc2 --Euro under pressure against other \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  amid thin liquidity\par \par \uc2 --Turkish lira rockets as \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  steps up pressure on \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  weakness\par \par \uc2 --Polish monetary policymaker says rates likely to be on hold in January and February\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par    By Jessica Mead \par    Of \f28 \uc2 \f2 DOW JONES NEWSWIRES\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 LONDON (\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 )--The euro sank to its lowest level against the Japanese yen since June 2001 in European hours Friday but extremely thin dealing conditions protected the single \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  from a broad-based selloff during the last trading session of 2011.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The euro remained under the cosh against other \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , hovering just above its 2011 lows against the dollar and slipping to its lowest level against the Swiss franc since Nov. 4, but investors were reluctant to add to any negative bets on the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  amid thin volumes.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "While most investors have probably pared back exposure approaching the end of the year, what positions there are appear to be biased to the downside, which may go some ways to explaining why the euro has been unable to extend losses," said Todd Elmer, \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  strategist at \f28 \uc2 \f2 Citigroup\f28 \uc2 \f2 .\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The fall in the euro against the yen also weighed on the dollar. It fell as low as Y77.28 against the Japanese \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , extending losses suffered in Asian hours on the back of last-minute settlement orders by Japanese exporters.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Overall, though, the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  markets remained very quiet. Even survey data showing a continued contraction in Chinese manufacturing activity in December failed to have any impact. "It caused a bit of interest, but nothing dramatic," said Steven Saywell, chief \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  strategist at \f28 \uc2 \f2 BNP Paribas\f28 \uc2 \f2  in London\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "People are sitting on their hands and waiting until the end of the year," he added.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Still, some excitement came from \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Turkey\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , where the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to support the wilting lira. The dollar dropped sharply from TRY1.92 to just under TRY1.86 by 1127 GMT as the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  sold foreign \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Elsewhere, the Polish zloty was weaker against the euro, which traded above PLN4.44, despite zloty-supportive \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by state-owned bank BGK. Anna Zielinska-Glebocka, a member of Poland's monetary policy council, said Poland's interest rates are likely to remain on hold in January and February as risks to the Polish economy balance each other out. She added that the zloty is currently undervalued but expects it will trail the single \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in 2012.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 At 1137 GMT, the euro was trading at $1.2944 against the dollar, compared with $1.2960 late Thursday in New York, according to trading system EBS. The dollar was at Y77.38 against the yen, compared with Y77.62, while the euro was at Y100.18 compared with Y100.70. Meanwhile, the pound was trading at $1.5451 against the dollar, compared with $1.5416 late Thursday in New York.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The ICE Dollar Index, which tracks the greenback against a basket of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , was at 80.364 compared with 80.371 late Thursday in New York.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -By Jessica Mead, \f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones Newswires\f28 \uc2 \f2 ; +44 (0) 20 7842 9256; jessica.mead@dowjones.com;@djfxtrader/@jessicacmead [ 30-12-11 1148GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020111230e7cu000ec\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
