\par\par \b \uc2 DJ Turkish Lira Hits Record Low Against Dollar In Risk Aversion\b0\par\par\uc2 By Erin McCarthy   \par \uc2 Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES   \par \uc2 169 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 29 Dezember 2011\par 00:38\par \uc2 Dow Jones Chinese Financial Wire\par \uc2 DJCFWE\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright (c) 2011, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 NEW YORK (\uc2 Dow Jones\uc2 )--The Turkish lira slid to an all-time low against the dollar Wednesday, as emerging European \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  suffered from a rush to the safe-haven U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The dollar shot up to TRY1.9158 against the lira, from TRY1.8994 late Tuesday, according to CQG. That marks the weakest level on record versus the dollar for Turkey's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The move came in line with the euro's slide against the dollar, as investors remain concerned about Italy, whose borrowing costs remain high despite a decent debt auction Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 Comments from \b \highlight22\uc2 Turkey\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor, who said the bank will \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  directly on the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market on exceptional days, further led investors to sell the lira, though in very thin trading.\par \par \uc2 -By Erin McCarthy, \uc2 Dow Jones Newswires\uc2 ; 212-416-2712; erin.mccarthy@dowjones.com\par \par \uc2 -0-\par \par \uc2 Copyright (c) 2011 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJCFWE0020111228e7cs00f4h\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
