\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 2-Turkish mkts fall after cbank, Fitch moves\b0\par\par\uc2 506 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 23 November 2011\par 09:41\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * Lira dips vs dollar after c.bank decision, Fitch downgrade\par \par \uc2 * C.bank holds policy rate as expected\par \par \uc2 * Bond yields rise, shares down\par \par \uc2 (Adds closing prices, quotes)\par \par \uc2 ISTANBUL, Nov 23 (Reuters) - The Turkish lira weakened and bond yields rose 9 basis points on Wednesday after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  left its policy rate and reserve requirements unchanged and Fitch cut Turkey's credit rating outlook to stable.\par \par \uc2 Fitch's decision to change the outlook on Turkey's BB+ long-term foreign and local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  ratings from positive, citing the challenge of reducing a large current account deficit and above-target inflation, dashed expectations the country could soon gain an investment grade rating. That hit the lira and stocks and pushed up benchmark government bond yields.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  kept the one-week repo rate at a record low of 5.75 percent at its monetary policy meeting and left overnight borrowing and lending rates unchanged as expected.\par \par \uc2 The lira closed at 1.8670 on the interbank market versus a previous close of 1.8480.\par \par \uc2 During intraday trade, the lira weakened to 1.8640 against the dollar after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  statement, from 1.8592 beforehand and extended its losses as far as 1.8745 after Fitch's statement.\par \par \uc2 "The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's decision was largely expected. However, those who were awaiting an increase in the lending rate or more tightening of lira liquidity bought dollars after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  announcement," said a trader at a bank in Istanbul.\par \par \uc2 "The Fitch statement affected the lira's value more. Now, nobody is thinking about an upgrade to investment grade anymore," he added.\par \par \uc2 There was also some disappointment that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  did not comment on \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy.\par \par \uc2 Against a euro-dollar basket the lira traded at 2.1858, weaker than a close of 2.1766. The lira touched its weakest level of 2.2274 versus the basket on Oct. 18, prompting the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  directly in the \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  market.\par \par \uc2 The yield on \b \highlight22\uc2 Turkey\b0 \highlight\uc2 's benchmark bond maturing in July 2013\par \par \uc2 closed at 10.6 percent, up from a previous close of 10.5 percent.\par \par \uc2 The benchmark yield rose to as high as 10.7 percent following Fitch's statement.\par \par \uc2 "Right after Fitch's statement, we saw some investors selling bonds. The benchmark yields rose to the same level after the Treasury's auctions. However, there isn't a serious outflow from the market. Volumes are low," said a fund manager.\par \par \uc2 Turkey's main share index fell 1.7 percent to 51,091.51 points, but outperformed the emerging markets index , which was down 2.6 percent.\par \par \uc2 "Fitch's statement had more of an effect on the stock market than the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's decision. A possible upgrade in the near term was our biggest expectation. Today's statement changed this story," said Gokhan Uskuay, strategy manager at Global Securities.\par \par \uc2 (Writing by Seltem Iyigun; Editing by Toby Chopra/Ruth Pitchford/Susan Fenton)\par \par \uc2 MARKETS-TURKEY/ (UPDATE 2)   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020111126e7bn0006c\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
