\par\par \b \uc2 Turkey Maintains Resistance To Lira Weakness\b0\par\par\uc2 501 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 19 Oktober 2011\par 13:15\par \uc2 Dow Jones Business News\par \uc2 DJON\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 LONDON -- Turkey's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  kept up its strong resistance to lira weakness Wednesday after announcing for the fourth time this month that it will offer a record $1.35 billion at its daily \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  selling auction.\par \par \uc2 The high volume on offer comes a day after \b \highlight22\uc2 Turkey\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  directly \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market for the first time in more than five years, as part of its latest efforts to stem weakness in the lira.\par \par \uc2 "At this stage the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is clearly concerned and keen to cap any further lira losses," said emerging market strategists at \uc2 UniCredit\uc2  in a note to clients.\par \par \uc2 So far, the measures have guided the lira over 1.5% higher against the dollar from the lows it hit earlier this week.\par \par \uc2 But with the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  running down reserves rapidly, concerns are rising it won't be able to keep up the fight, market participants say.\par \par \uc2 "It would be relatively unrealistic to expect that it had sufficient \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves to prevent a depreciation of the lira over an extended period of time," said Thu Lan Nguyen, an emerging market strategist at \uc2 Commerzbank\uc2  in Frankfurt.\par \par \uc2 Unless you have unlimited ammunition, it will be difficult to prevent the lira from further weakness, she said. "All you can do is smooth out losses, you cannot prevent a depreciation," she added.\par \par \uc2 The lira, like several other emerging market \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , has come under intense selling pressure in recent weeks as a toxic combination of global economy fears and escalating euro-zone debt worries led investors to fold their bets in emerging markets on a colossal scale.\par \par \uc2 Until now, the bank had avoided \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  directly on the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market and had instead been selling dollars at a daily auction to stem the depreciation of the lira.\par \par \uc2 But continued selling pressure spurred its first \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  since May 2006, something which market participants expect to continue, for the time being at least.\par \par \uc2 "Turkey's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is likely to carry on with sizeable daily auctions and direct \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  for the time being, keeping lower \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserve requirement ratios in its pocket for now," said Turker Hamzaoglu of \uc2 Bank of America\uc2 Merrill Lynch\uc2 , adding that in 2006 the bank called an emergency meeting and raised rates 225 basis points in three \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Since November 2010, the lira has fallen 30% against the dollar after the bank began an unorthodox monetary policy that cut the benchmark interest rate to deter speculative inflows while increasing bank reserve ratios to slow a gathering credit boom.\par \par \uc2 Eyes will be on Turkey's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's interest rate decision, which is due Thursday at 1100 GMT. Analysts expect the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to keep interest rates and the reserve requirement ratios on lira and foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  holdings, unchanged.\par \par \uc2 -By Clare Connaghan and Yeliz Candemir, Dow Jones Newswires; +44 (0) 20 7842 9496, clare.connaghan@dowjones.com\par \par \uc2 (Joe Parkinson in Istanbul contributed to this item.) [ 10-19-11 0715ET ]\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJON000020111019e7aj0003n\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
