\par\par \b \uc2 News Highlights: Top Economic Stories Of The Day\b0\par\par\uc2 736 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 Oktober 2011\par 20:00\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par TOP STORIES \par  \par US STOCKS RISE FOLLOWING EARNINGS, DATA \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 U.S. stocks are up as investors react to a plethora of quarterly results, continued concern over Europe's debt crisis and a domestic economy facing inflation pressures.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par BERNANKE SEES EVOLUTION IN POLICY AFTER CRISIS \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Lessons learned in the financial crisis suggest the Federal Reserve will need to revise, but not abandon, how it approaches monetary policy in the future, Fed Chairman Ben Bernanke says in a speech. He didn't comment on the economic and interest rate outlook.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par GOLDMAN SWINGS TO LOSS ON INVESTMENT LOSSES \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Investment banking giant posts a 3Q loss of $393 million, or 84c a share, hurt by stiff markdowns in the value of its massive lending and investing portfolio. Investment banking revenue slumps 33%, while net revenue slides 60% to $3.59 billion. Shares up 2%.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par BANK OF AMERICA SWINGS TO PROFIT; REVENUE UP \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Second-largest U.S. bank posts 3Q profit of $6.23 billion, or 56c a share, compared with a year-earlier loss of $7.3 billion, or 77c a share, and revenue grows 6.6% to $28.45 billion. \f28 \uc2 \f2 J.P. Morgan Chase\f28 \uc2 \f2  passes BofA in assets. Shares up 5%.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par US PRODUCER PRICES UP; HOUSING INDEX RISES \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 U.S. wholesale prices rise 0.8% in September on the back of higher costs for gasoline, food and household detergents. In a separate report, US home builders' sentiment rises to the highest level in 17 months in October.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par CHINA GROWTH SLOWS, POLICY OUTLOOK UNCLEAR \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China's economic growth slowed in the third quarter but remained at a relatively healthy pace, adding to evidence that the Chinese economy is headed for a soft landing.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par FRENCH FIN MIN SAYS WORKING ON 'STRONG' PROPOSALS FOR SUMMIT \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 France is working on a "strong, structured, stable" response to the euro-zone debt crisis, Finance Minister Francois Baroin says ahead of this weekend's European summit.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par SANCTIONS AN OPTION FOR EMU PACT SAYS TRICHET \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The European Union treaty should include sanctions for countries that fail to comply with deficit and debt limits, European \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  President Jean-Claude Trichet says in an interview.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 JOHNSON & JOHNSON\f28 \uc2 \f2  NET DROPS 6% ON WRITEDOWNS \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Health-care products titan's 3Q profit dips to $3.2 billion, or $1.15 a share, after taking writedowns on its pending Synthes acquisition. Absent items, earnings per share top estimates. Revenue increases 7% to $16 billion.\f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 TURKEY CENTRAL BANK INTERVENES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  TO BOOST LIRA \par  \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Turkey\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank intervenes\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  directly to support the lira for the first time in five years, taking on skeptical \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  markets after an earlier U.S. dollar auction failed to lift the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par  \par    ======== DOW JONES NEWSWIRES ANALYSIS AND COMMENTARY ======== \par  \par Heard on the Street \par GOLDMAN'S JEKYLL PAINTS MR HYDE RED \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The securities house known as \f28 \uc2 \f2 Goldman Sachs\f28 \uc2 \f2  didn't have a terrible quarter--in fact, it was decent considering all the market upheaval. Unfortunately, the hedge-fund/private-equity shop also known as \f28 \uc2 \f2 Goldman Sachs\f28 \uc2 \f2  took a beating.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par The Wall Street Journal \par CHINA'S GROWTH GETS HELP FROM DOMESTIC DEMAND \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Chinese economic data suggest a nation that has long relied on exports is getting more help from domestic demand--a potential benefit for the global economy as Europe grapples with its debt crisis and U.S. growth sputters.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Interview \par EURO CAN'T SURVIVE IN CURRENT FORM SAYS \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  CONCEPTS CHAIRMAN \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The euro can't survive in its current form, but its stubborn strength has contributed to a "terrible" year for those seeking profits from \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  trading, according to John Taylor, founder and chairman of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Concepts.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Heard on the Street \par PORTUGAL'S GROWING CHALLENGE \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Portugal's economic story is beginning to sound unpleasantly familiar, as the new Social Democrat government, which took power in June, says the country's recession will be deeper than forecast as more austerity is needed.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par   ============ MARKETS ACTION ============ \par  \par US STOCKS RISE FOLLOWING EARNINGS, DATA; FINANCIALS STRENGTHEN \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 U.S. stocks rise following earnings, data.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par GROWTH WORRIES HELP TREASURYS RECOVER FROM PPI SETBACK \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Treasurys are nudged higher by global economic worries.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par EUR PARES LOSSES; BUYERS SEEN AT $1.3620 \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Euro pares losses as buyers step up.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par CRUDE FUTURES HIGHER AS US STOCKS STAGE RALLY \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Oil futures higher as traders weigh stock rally.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par COMEX GOLD PARES LOSSES AS DOLLAR EASES \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Gold pares its earlier losses and silver pushes into positive territory as dollar eases. [ 18-10-11 1800GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 1030 1804 4180  \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020111018e7ai0018t\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
