\par\par \b \uc2 EMERGING MARKETS-China, euro zone fears snap winning run\b0\par\par\uc2 890 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 Oktober 2011\par 13:59\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * China GDP, French rating warning spark 2 pct emerging-share drop\par \par \uc2 * Turkish \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  launches \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  auction after lira slide\par \par \uc2 * Hungarian forint falls, debt insurance spikes up on rating fears\par \par \uc2 By Sebastian Tong\par \par \uc2 LONDON, Oct 18 (Reuters) - Disappointing Chinese third-quarter GDP growth and a warning on France's credit rating sent emerging markets reeling on Tuesday while Turkey's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  launched a \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  auction to steady the lira from a record low to the euro/dollar basket.\par \par \uc2 The darkened outlook for the global economy knocked Russian stocks and its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  lower while Hungary's risk premiums rose and its forint slid on fears of an imminent ratings cut.\par \par \uc2 Emerging shares dropped 2.2 percent by 1130 GMT, more than double the one-percent loss on developed markets\par \par \uc2 and snapping a nine-session rally that saw the benchmark leap over 14 percent to Monday's four-week highs.\par \par \uc2 Optimism for a speedy resolution to the euro zone debt crisis all but evaporated after \uc2 Moody's\uc2  warned it may slap a negative outlook on France's Aaa credit rating in the next three months should bailout costs stretch its budget excessively.\par \par \uc2 "The market had clearly been a little too optimistic about a solution to the euro zone debt crisis. This is a complicated problem and with so many voices, the solution will take time and be painful," said Gaelle Blanchard, emerging markets strategist at \uc2 Societe Generale\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 "Even if the Europeans manage to come up with a unanimous plan with strong measures, how will credit agencies react to the further burden on their government budgets? We could have a negative impact on that front even if we have good news on debt resolution."\par \par \uc2 Data showing China's economic expansion slowing to its weakest pace since early 2009 in the third quarter further renewed fears of a global slowdown that were alleviated last week after retail, manufacturing and employment readings showed signs of improvement in the U.S. economy.\par \par \uc2 Adding to the gloom, the European Bank for Reconstruction and Development cut its forecast for 2012 GDP growth in its 29 countries of \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  which includes Central and Eastern Europe as well as Central Asia.\par \par \uc2 Steep share losses in the Asian session, which saw Hong Kong's Hang Seng plummet over 4 percent and the Shanghai's key stock index drop more than 2 percent, moderated slightly by the European trade.\par \par \uc2 The Thomson Reuters Emerging European stock index\par \par \uc2 eased 0.3 percent lower though Polish and Hungarian shares were 1 percent lower.\par \par \uc2 Weaker oil prices kept Russia's dollar RTS Index down for its second day while the rouble-denominated share index\par \par \uc2 waned from Monday's three-week highs.\par \par \uc2 TURKEY ACTS, HUNGARIAN WORRIES\par \par \uc2 The threat of weaker Chinese demand for commodities also weighed on the rouble, which fell nearly 1 percent against its euro/dollar basket and slipped from Monday's four-week high versus the greenback .\par \par \uc2 Emerging \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  were otherwise mixed with the Polish zloty stabilising after weakening three straight sessions against the euro and Romania's leu at a two-week low versus the common \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Israel's shekel drooped half a percentage point after touching a six-week high against the dollar on Monday.\par \par \uc2 Hungary's forint slid for its fourth straight session\par \par \uc2 while the cost of insuring the country's sovereign debt for five years rose some 10 basis points higher from the previous close.\par \par \uc2 Officials from credit rating agencies \uc2 Standard & Poor's\uc2  and \uc2 Moody's\uc2  are due in Budapest this month in meetings that BoA-\uc2 Merrill Lynch\uc2  has warned could lead to the loss of its investment grade status by one agency.\par \par \uc2 BoA-\uc2 Merrill Lynch\uc2  estimates that Hungary's total financing needs in 2012 is at 13.2 billion euros, up from 12.3 billion this year. Foreign investors now hold a significant chunk of local and foreign-\b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  Hungarian bonds but their exposure will need to increase further as the ability of local players to absorb new paper is limited, the bank said.\par \par \uc2 "However, this could prove challenging given the potentially lower rating and an unfavourable global backdrop," it warned.\par \par \uc2 A $1.35 billion \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  selling auction helped to steady the lira further after a two-percent fall versus the dollar on Monday.\par \par \uc2 Earlier, the unit sank to a record low of 2.2261 against its euro/dollar basket on high corporate demand to meet import payments .\par \par \uc2 JPMorgan\uc2  is recommending a short dollar/lira trade, with an entry of 1.87 and a target level of 1.79 with stop losses triggered at 1.91.\par \par \uc2 "In the short-run, the (Turkish \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 ) has the determination and capacity to support the lira in periods of risk aversion. Turkey has been amongst the most determined to cap depreciation pressure on the lira, particularly since the start of October, with both verbal and physical \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  intensifying," it said in a note.\par \par \uc2 On Monday, \b \highlight22\uc2 Turkey\b0 \highlight\uc2  defied market volatility to raise $1 billion with a 10-year dollar-denominated bond that attracted demand totalling over $3 billion.\par \par \uc2 Turkey's share of the \uc2 JPMorgan\uc2  EMBI hard-\b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  bond benchmark traded 6 bps wider over U.S. Treasuries, underperforming the index which was 5 bps wider at 371 bps.\par \par \uc2 (Reporting by Sebastian Tong; editing by Anna Willard)\par \par \uc2 MARKETS-EMERGING   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020111021e7ai000z9\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
