\par\par \b \uc2 Emerging-Market  \highlight22\uc2 Currencies \highlight\uc2  Mixed, Debt Steady With Euro-Zone Focus\b0\par\par\uc2 585 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 Oktober 2011\par 22:42\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 -Global growth worries, euro-zone crisis continue to dominate riskier assets' performance\par \par \uc2 -\b \highlight22\uc2 Turkey\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market\par \par \uc2 -Emerging-market \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  mixed\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    By Erin McCarthy \par    Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 NEW YORK (Dow Jones)--Emerging-market \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  were mixed Tuesday after euro-zone officials dismissed reports of an agreement to bolster the euro zone's rescue fund, while debt was little changed.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Emerging-market \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  had been slightly down for most of the session, after Chinese data showing slower-than-expected third quarter growth and ongoing euro-zone sovereign debt crisis worries pressured riskier assets.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Reports that France and Germany had agreed to expand the region's bailout fund to EUR2 trillion triggered a reversal in some of those \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  late in the session. But those gains were limited as various euro-zone sources refuted the report and said no deal on the bailout fund would be reached until Friday.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Still, market watchers warn that euro-zone policymakers must take more decisive action in order to ease investor jitters.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "The near term concern is that without some solution we're looking at a more likelihood of a [Greek] default," said Brian Dolan, chief \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  strategist at \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .com. "If you get one [default] it raises the question of a whole domino effect."\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The risk premium on the \f28 \uc2 \f2 J.P. Morgan\f28 \uc2 \f2  Emerging Markets Bond Index Global, or Embig, tightened by three basis points to 408 basis points over Treasurys. In price terms, its index fell 0.1%.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Euro-zone worries have weighed more heavily on emerging-market \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , especially in emerging Europe. Turkey's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  stepped into the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market Tuesday to support its falling \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , while other \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 ' gains were muted.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Turkish lira advanced about 0.4% against the dollar, which changed hands at TRY1.8573 late Tuesday, according to CQG. Earlier, \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Turkey\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  directly \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market for the first time in more than five years, its latest effort to prop up its embattled \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . It also sold $750 million at its daily \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 -selling auction. Investors wary of Turkey's large current account deficit and its exposure to the euro zone continue to sell the lira in times of risk aversion.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Eyes are also on Brazil's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , which is widely expected to cut its Selic base interest rate by 50 basis points Wednesday, to 11.5% from 12%. That has pressured the real, but the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  got a last-minute boost from heightened hopes for a euro-zone plan and a late-day rally in U.S. stocks. The dollar fell 0.4% to BRL1.7530 from BRL1.7600 late Monday, according to CQG. On the Embig, Brazil's spread was little changed, just two basis points tighter at 230 basis points over Treasurys.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Mexican peso led gainers, largely tracking the rise in U.S. equities. The dollar slipped 0.8% to MXN13.3755 against the peso, which often serves as a proxy for risk among investors. Chile's peso, meanwhile, tumbled more than 1% on lower international copper prices and fears of slowing growth in China, a main source for commodity demand. Chile's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  often tracks the red metal's prices, since the Andean nation is the world largest copper producer.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -By Erin McCarthy, Dow Jones Newswires; 212-416-2712; erin.mccarthy@dowjones.com\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -Joe Parkinson and Clare Connaghan contributed to this article. [ 18-10-11 2042GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020111018e7ai001ag\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
