\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Turkey Central Bank \highlight\uc2  Declines To Give Amount Of  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 186 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 Oktober 2011\par 15:30\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 LONDON (Dow Jones)--\b \highlight22\uc2 Turkey\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  stepped up its fight to support the lira Tuesday by directly \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  confirmed.\par \par \uc2 The Turkish lira jumped almost 1% against the dollar after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  bought its local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , as part of its latest measures to support the battered \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The lira, like several other emerging market \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , has come under intense selling pressure in recent weeks as a toxic combination of global economy fears and escalating euro-zone debt worries led investors to fold their bets in emerging markets on a colossal scale.\par \par \uc2 Up until now the bank had avoided \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  directly on the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, instead it had been selling dollars at a daily auction to stem depreciation of the lira.\par \par \uc2 By 1325 GMT the dollar was trading at TRY1.8552 against the lira, down from TRY1.8690 immediately prior to the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 -By Clare Connaghan, Dow Jones Newswires; +44 (0) 20 7842 9496, clare.connaghan@dowjones.com (Gary Stride contributed to this item.) [ 18-10-11 1342GMT ]\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020111018e7ai0010z\par }\page {\par