\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 2-Turkish c.bank  \highlight22\uc2 intervenes \highlight\uc2 , boosts ailing lira\b0\par\par\uc2 549 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 Oktober 2011\par 15:15\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * C.bank sells more than $1 billion to support lira\par \par \uc2 * C.bank says "speculative behaviour" behind lira moves\par \par \uc2 * Lira firms to below 1.85 before slipping back\par \par \uc2 (Adds analyst comments, background)\par \par \uc2 By Seltem Iyigun\par \par \uc2 ISTANBUL, Oct 18 (Reuters) - The Turkish \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  sold over $1 billion to support an ailing lira on Tuesday, and said it was stung into action by unhealthy \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  moves based on speculation.\par \par \uc2 The bank began by selling $750 million at its daily \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  selling auction, but when that failed to relieve pressure on the lira the bank \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  directly with sales exceeding $600 million, traders said.\par \par \uc2 The lira firmed to below 1.85 against the dollar after the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  from 1.8675 beforehand and compared with Monday's interbank closing level of 1.8520.\par \par \uc2 However it subsequently lost ground back to 1.86, bringing losses this year against the dollar to 17 percent. \b \highlight22\uc2 Intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  continued around 1435 GMT. The yield on the benchmark bond fell to 8.50 from 8.60 percent and the share index ended up 0.5 percent.\par \par \uc2 The lira has come under considerable selling pressure in recent months, losing almost as much as 20 percent against the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , as a result of a flight from risk.\par \par \uc2 Daily \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2 -selling auctions have been at the centre of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's response to the depreciation and it has sold more than $5 billion since it started the auctions on Aug 5.\par \par \uc2 The bank said in a statement it could hold a high-volume \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2 -selling auction on Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 "Selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is being carried out in the market due to unhealthy exchange rate price formations, resulting from speculative behaviour linked to a loss of market depth," the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENTION\b0 \highlight\uc2  SUSTAINABLE?\par \par \uc2 Analysts questioned how long the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  could maintain such \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 "I don't know how long the bank could continue this way. If people start questioning the sufficiency of its \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves, then the real speculation could start," said Mehmet Besimoglu, chief economist at Oyak Securities.\par \par \uc2 Turkish \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  gross \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves stood at $85.1 billion lira on Oct. 7, down from $93 billion at the end of July.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  has heightened investor interest in Thursday's monetary policy committee meeting amid speculation it could take further measures to support the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 "In its monthly meeting, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  may consider increasing its borrowing rate in order to implement a tight monetary policy," Besimoglu said.\par \par \uc2 In a Reuters poll conducted last week, all 14 analysts polled forecast the bank would keep its policy rate at a record low of 5.75 percent. One forecast a reduction of 50 basis points in required reserve ratios (RRR)and another forecast a hike of the overnight borrowing rate.\par \par \uc2 The Turkish economy, which surged close to 10 percent in the first half, is expected to slow dramatically in the next year and the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has said it would loosen monetary policy if the slowdown becomes more pronounced.\par \par \uc2 At the same time, the lira depreciation has fuelled fears about rising inflation which were ignited by recent public sector price hikes and consumer tax increases.\par \par \uc2 (Reporting by Seltem Iyigun; Writing by Daren Butler)\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 TURKEY\b0 \highlight\uc2 -CBANK/\b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENTION\b0 \highlight\uc2   (UPDATE 2)   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020111018e7ai000ra\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
