\par\par \b \uc2 DJ UPDATE:  \highlight22\uc2 Turkey \highlight\uc2  Econ Min: Ctrl Bk  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2  'Appropriate'\b0\par\par\uc2 336 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 13 Oktober 2011\par 18:42\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2011, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 -- \b \highlight22\uc2 Turkey\b0 \highlight\uc2  economy minister says moves by \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  were appropriate\par \par \uc2 -- Says moves helped temper "speculative attacks"\par \par \uc2 -- "Devaluation" of \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is also important\par \par \uc2 (Adds comment, background)\par \par \uc2 MADRID (Dow Jones)--\b \highlight22\uc2 Turkey\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was right to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets to help temper speculative attacks against the lira, Turkish Economy Minister Zafer Caglayan said at a conference here Thursday.\par \par \uc2 "The bank \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  at the right time and speculative attacks were killed off," he said. "The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , when is necessary...does its work in an appropriate way."\par \par \uc2 Last week, the bank took a series of actions to stem the fall of the lira and curb volatility. The bank cut reserve requirements on lira and foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  deposits, sold hefty amounts in its daily dollar auctions and allowed banks to use foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  to satisfy more of the reserve requirements for lira deposits.\par \par \uc2 On Thursday, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  didn't hold a \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  auction and declined to explain why. But it sold $70 million at its daily \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  auction Wednesday, after offering to sell as much as $140 million.\par \par \uc2 The amount up for auction was less than the $350 million offered at Tuesday's auction and much lower than the record $1.35 billion offered at both Wednesday's and Thursday's auctions last week. However, the bank only went on to sell $750 million and $350 million, respectively, on those days.\par \par \uc2 Despite his support for the bank's moves to put a floor under the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Caglayan also said he that what he called "devaluation," a weakening of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , was important for Turkey and other countries.\par \par \uc2 However, lira depreciation is stoking investor concerns over the country's inflation, which the government expects to reach around 8% this year.\par \par \uc2 --By Ilan Brat, Dow Jones Newswires; +34 618 526 915; ilan.brat@dowjones.com. Yeliz Candemir contributed to this story from Istanbul.\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 October 13, 2011 12:42 ET (16:42 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020111013e7ad004jm\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
