\par\par \b \uc2 RPT-ANALYSIS-Turkey defending lira with limited  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  ammunition\b0\par\par\uc2 By Sujata Rao and Seltem Iyigun  \par \uc2 983 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 Oktober 2011\par 07:00\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 (Repeats without changes to text)\par \par \uc2 ISTANBUL, Oct 6 (Reuters) - Turkey has upped the ante in defence of the lira, but with hard cash reserves far smaller than those of many developing economy peers, \b \highlight22\uc2 FX intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  may not be feasible for long should investors resume their exodus from emerging markets.\par \par \uc2 Faced with year-to-date lira losses of almost 20 percent to the dollar and rising inflation, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  this week mounted its most aggressive defence of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  yet, selling a record $1.1 billion on Wednesday and Thursday and making changes to banks' reserve requirements.\par \par \uc2 The action succeeded in lifting the lira well off record lows. But any further \b \highlight22\uc2 FX interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  will put \b \highlight22\uc2 Turkey\b0 \highlight\uc2  in serious danger of depleting a reserve stash that is its primary buffer against a large balance of payments deficit.\par \par \uc2 Reserves stand now at around $85 billion, far short of the hundreds of billions of dollars held by other comparable emerging market countries and down more than 10 percent from July as a result of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's daily dollar auctions.\par \par \uc2 "This speed of reserve drawdown is not sustainable," said Manik Narain, emerging markets strategist at \uc2 UBS\uc2  in London. "Turkey's reserves in terms of external debt coverage or import coverage are among the the lowest in emerging markets."\par \par \uc2 In contrast, South Korean \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  throughout September cost it $9 billion but made a dent of less than 3 percent in its reserves, the world's eighth-largest.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  data shows $132 billion in external debt payments due in the coming year, mostly private sector. Add in the huge current account gap and the liability mounts to over $200 billion -- more than double its current reserve level.\par \par \uc2 Turkey in fact is one of only four emerging countries whose \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves are insufficient to cover annual trade balance needs and maturing short-term debt, a \uc2 UBS\uc2  study shows. The other countries in this position are Bulgaria, Latvia and Belarus.\par \par \uc2 "The Turkish \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  ... is not Brazil or Korea which have a lot more firepower," said Alia Yousuf, a bond portfolio manager with ACPI Investments in London.\par \par \uc2 "If this (reserves decline) continues it will obviously lead to more uneasiness with investors. Ultimately if global market uncertainty remains, funding the Turkish current account deficit will become an increasing worry."\par \par \uc2 BANK UNEASY?\par \par \uc2 BNP Paribas\uc2  analysts note that the gross reserves-imports ratio stands at 37 percent while the reserves to short-term debt ratio is at 98 percent, just above levels it says are mentioned by the bank in its reserve management guidelines.\par \par \uc2 "Our back-of-the envelope calculation yields that if the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  sells $10 billion more, all \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserve ratios will decline to or below their critical levels," BNP told clients.\par \par \uc2 Though the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  deliberately engineered a depreciation in the lira in the early part of the year, it has appeared increasingly uncomfortable with the scale and pace of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's fall.\par \par \uc2 On Thursday it attempted to soothe analysts' worries, saying in a presentation that its reserve position was quite strong, judging by the ratio of reserves to short term \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  debt.\par \par \uc2 But signs are it is uneasy; hence the decision to allow banks to hold more reserves in dollars, a step that may add $3.6 billion to its own coffers.\par \par \uc2 But the coming months may well see a further rise in dollar demand from Turkish banks and corporates which borrowed heavily overseas to fund booming domestic growth but will see a record $132 billion come due in the coming year, including coupons.\par \par \uc2 RBS compared the predicament to Russia's in 2008, when a third of \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves vanished in the rouble's defence.\par \par \uc2 "Russia suffered badly back then because it had $160-80 billion in external debt liabilities falling due; and yet it got into trouble even with $590 billion in \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves, which now underscores the risks in Turkey's case," RBS said.\par \par \uc2 RESERVES OR RATES\par \par \uc2 So apart from praying for a quick resolution of the euro zone crisis, what can Turkey's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  do next?\par \par \uc2 Tufan Comert, strategist at Garanti Securities in Istanbul said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  could try for a swap line with the U.S. Federal Reserve, which stepped in to provide liquidity to many emerging central banks in 2008. Or it could lend dollars to banks on \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  deposit instead of selling, he said.\par \par \uc2 What markets would really like to see is an interest rate rise. Turkey's policy rate, the one-week repo rate, is at 5.75 percent, a negative rate in real terms, though the one-year bond yield is still in positive territory at 8.3 percent.\par \par \uc2 Yet the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  admitted this week end-2011 inflation would be significantly above-target.\par \par \uc2 But a rate rise would mark an immense U-turn for the bank which has eased policy several times this year to engineer lira depreciation. It would argue a rate hike now will put Turkey at a disadvantage, given growth at home and abroad is slowing.\par \par \uc2 "I would have liked to have seen the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  defending the lira with interest rate weapons as well, rather than only \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," said Namik Aksel, chief executive of HSBC Asset Management \b \highlight22\uc2 Turkey\b0 \highlight\uc2 . "Obviously this policy is a risk but they do have a point. Growth is going to be the main driver in 2012."\par \par \uc2 He too reckons no more than $5-$10 billion can be spent from now in the lira's defence. After that circumstances may force the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's hand -- the bank's strategy clearly hinges on a reversal of the global bearish market sentiment.\par \par \uc2 "I do believe they may hike overnight borrowing rates if we see another round of heavy sell-off," Aksel added.\par \par \uc2 (Editing by Catherine Evans)\par \par \uc2 EMERGING-TURKEY/LIRA (ANALYSIS)  \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020111010e7a70007k\par }\par \b \uc2 Zusammenfassung der Suche\b0\par \par  \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx2000\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx9072\pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 \uc2 Text\cell \pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 \li50\uc2 (foreign exchange or fx or forex or currenc*) and (interven* or operation*) and (Turkey near10 interven*) and (rst=trtw or rst=tprw or rst=tdjw) and (central bank o